1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://de-academic.com/dic.nsf/dewiki/218434#Adelserhebungen
2 CONT
2 CONT Albrecht von Buxthoeven (um 1165-1229), Bischof von Riga.
2 CONT Hermann I. von Buxthoeven (1163-1248), Bischof von Dorpat.
2 CONT _____________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann_of_Dorpat '''Hermann of Dorpat'''] (or '''Hermann I''', or '''Hermann von Buxhövden''') (1163–1248) was the first 
2 CONT * https://et.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann_von_Buxh%C3%B6vden
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince-bishop Prince-Bishop] of the 
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bishopric_of_Dorpat Bishopric of Dorpat] (1224–1248) within the 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terra_Mariana#Livonian_Confederation Livonian Confederation].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hermann hailed from''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bexh%C3%B6vede Bexhövede] (now a part of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loxstedt Loxstedt], Lower Saxony) in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Saxony Duchy of Saxo
2 CONC ny], and was also known as "Hermann of Buxhoeveden" and other variations, such as Buxhöwden and Buxthoeven. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the brother''' of Bishop [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_of_Riga Albert of Riga], who used his influence against King [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valdemar_II_of_Denmark Valdemar II of Denmark] to place the [http
2 CONC s://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livonian_Brothers_of_the_Sword Livonian Brothers of the Sword] in medieval Estonia. From 10 April 1220 – 21 July 1224, Hermann was the Bishop of Leal (Lihula), after which he took over the Bishopric of Do
2 CONC rpat.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hermann founded the''' cathedral of Tartu (Dorpat) and led the Roman Catholic crusading army in the 1242 [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_on_the_Ice Battle of the Ice], which was won by the Russian Orthodox [https://en.wik
2 CONC ipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Nevsky Alexander Nevsky] of Novgorod. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It has also been suggested''' that he founded the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raseborg_Castle Raseborg Castle] at the southern coast of Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Legacy===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hermann was the progenitor''' of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buxhoeveden_family House of Buxhoeveden], a Baltic German family whose members entered Prussian, Swedish, and Russian service over the following centuries. The
2 CONC ir descendants live in Germany, Finland, Estonia and Russia today.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.buxhoeveden.net/index.php?link=3
2 CONT
2 CONT Vikipedia: https://et.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buxhoeveden
2 CONT
2 CONT Vikipedia2: https://et.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann_von_Buxh%C3%B6vden
