2 CONT from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Heinrich von Bokholt ( bl. 1227-1250 in Lübeck ) was councilor of the Hanseatic city of Lübeck.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich von Bokholt was the son of the Lübeck councilor Richard von Bokholt. He is occupied for the period from 1227 to 1250 as a councilman in Lübeck. For the first time he dived into a Pope Gregory IX. arranged on appeal by the
2 CONC  Bishop of Lübeck investigation against him and the Lubeck''' councilor Hartwich of Parchim ['''1] on where it comes to appropriate use or unauthorized use of donations for the construction of the Lübeck Cathedral went - Ingestuur
2 CONC  Ds. MG Muller
