2 CONT                                   o F4. Maria, heiress of Galicia-Lvov, *bef 1293, +11.1.1341; m.before 1310 Pr Trojden I of Masovia (+13.3.1341)
2 CONT                                   o F5. [parentage unproven] Anastasia, +1364/65; m.ca 1320 Pr Alexander I of Tver (+28.10.1339)
2 CONT                             * E2. Anastasia, +12.3.1335; m.before 1301 Pr Ziemowit of Poland (+1309/14)
2 CONT                             * E3. Svyatoslava, a nun, +1302
2 CONT                       # D3. Roman, Duke of Slonim and Novogrudok (1255-60), *ca 1230, +ca 1261; 1m: 27.6.1252 (div 1253) Gertrud of Austria (*ca 1288, +24.4.1299); 2m: ca 1255 Elena Glebovna of Volkovysk (+aft 1288)
2 CONT                             * E1. [1m.] Maria; m.N, a son of ban Stefan of Zagreb
2 CONT                             * E2. [2m.] Vasilko, Pr of Slonim, *ca 1256, +after 1282; he may (or may not) have been grandfather of Pr Daniel Ostrogski
2 CONT                             * E3. [parentage uncertain] Mikhail, Pr of Drutsk; his alleged descendants include Princes Drucki-Lubecki, Drutskoy-Sokolinsky, Babichev, and Putyatin
2 CONT                       # D4. Mstislav, Duke of Lutsk (1265-89), Duke of Volynia (1289-aft 1300), +aft 1300; m.ca 1253 N, a dau.of khan Teigak of the Cumans
2 CONT                             * E1. Danylo, +1280-1300
2 CONT                             * E2. Vladimir III, Duke of Volynia, +1315
2 CONT                       # D5. Ioann Shvarn "the Lightning", Duke of Chelm (1264-69), Great Duke of Lithuania (1268-69), +1269, bur Chelm; m.1255 N, a dau.of Duke Mindaugas of Lithuania
2 CONT                       # D6. Pereyaslava, +12.4.1283; m.ca 1248 Pr Ziemowit of Masovia (*1224, +23.6.1262)
2 CONT                       # D7. Ustinia; m.1250/51 Pr Andrei II of Vladimir-Suzdal (+1264)
2 CONT                       # D8. Sofia; m.1259 Gf Heinrich V von Schwarzburg-Blankenburg (+1287)
2 CONT                 + C3. [2m.] Vasilko, Duke of Belz (1207-11), Duke of Brest (1221-31), Duke of Volynya (1231-69), *1203, +1269; 1m: 1226 Dobrava of Vladimir (+after 5.12.1247); 2m: after 1248 a Polish princess (+1265)
2 CONT                       # D1. Vladimir, Duke of Volynya (1269-89), *after 1248, +10.12.1289; m.1263 Elena Romanovna of Briansk (+after 1288)
2 CONT                       # D2. Olga, *after 1248, +after 10.12.1288; m.1259/61 Andrei Vsevolodovich of Chernigov (+after 1262)
2 CONT           o B2. Svyatoslav, Pr of Brest, +1172/83
2 CONT           o B3. Vsevolod, Pr of Belz (1170-95), Pr of Volynia (1187-88), +IV.1195
2 CONT                 + C1. Alexandr, Pr of Belz (1195-1208)+(1215-33), Pr of Volynya (1208-15), +after 1234; m.N, a dau.of Pr Vladimir IV of Smolensk
2 CONT                       # D1. Vsevolod III, Pr of Belz, +after 1245
2 CONT                             * E1. [parentage uncertain] Gremislava, *bef 1284, +13.9.1302; m.ca 1280 Pr Boleslaw I of Opole (+14.5.1313)
2 CONT                       # D2. Anastasia; 1m: 1245/47 Pr Boleslaw I of Masovia (+25.2.1248); 2m: after 1248 Dymitr, a Hungarian boyar
2 CONT                 + C2. Vsevolod, Pr of Cherven (1207-1212), Pr of Belz (1211-15), +after 1215
2 CONT     * A2. Yaroslav, Pr of Novgorod (1148-54), Pr of Lutsk (1154-80), Grand Pr of Kiev (XII.1173-VI.1174), +1180; he was possibly married to a Przemyslid princess
2 CONT           o B1. Ingvar, Pr of Lutsk (1180-1220), Great Pr of Kiev (1202-04), +1214/24
2 CONT                 + C1. Izyaslav, Pr of Dorogobuzh, +k.a.Kalka River 16.6.1223
2 CONT                 + C2. Yaroslav, Pr of Lutsk and Przemysl, +after 1239
2 CONT                       # D1. Boris, Pr of Medzhibizh, +after 1234; he was putative ancestor of Princes Bolkhovskoy
2 CONT                 + C3. Vladimir, Pr of Kamenets, +1229
2 CONT                       # D1. Izyaslav, Pr of Kamenets, +after 1255
2 CONT                 + C4. Gremislava, +1258; m.1207 Pr Leszek of Krakow (*1186/87, +23.11.1227)
2 CONT           o B2. Vsevolod, Pr of Dorogobuzh (1180-86), +after 1209; m.ca 1167 Malfrida of Turov
2 CONT           o B3. Izyaslav, Pr of Shumsk (1180-96), +II.1196
2 CONT           o B4. Mstislav "Nyemiy" "the Mute", Pr of Peresopnitsa (1180-1220), Pr of Lutsk (1220-26), +1226/27
2 CONT                 + C1. Ivan, Pr of Lutsk and Czartorysk (1226-27)
2 CONT           o B5. Anastasia
2 CONT     * A3. Yaropolk, Pr of Shumsk, +7.3.1168/70; m.1164/66 Maria Svyatoslavna of Chernigov (*1149 +1189)
2 CONT           o B1. Vasilko, Pr of Shumsk (1168-80), Pr of Dorohychyn (1180-82), *bef 1151, +after 1182; m.1172/73 N of Poland (+after 1178)
2 CONT     * A4. a daughter, fl 1143; m.1143/44 Pr Rogvolod II of Polotsk (+7.5.1171)
