2 CONC Hungary (-after 12 Dec 1201).  The Chronicon Polono-Silesiacum refers to, but does not name, the daughters of Mieszko III, naming (second in the list) "dux Saxonie" as his son-in-law[576].  A 13th century genealogy refers to the w
2 CONC ife of "Berenhardum [filius Albertus de Hanhalde marchio]" as "ducis Polonie filiam"[577].  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names "Iuttam filiam Mesechonis ducis Polonie" as wife of "Bernardus dux Saxonie"[578].  Duke Bernhard & his
2 CONC  wife had five children:  1.         MAGNUS (-young).  The Cronica Principum Saxonie names (in order) "Albertum ducem Saxonie et Henricum comitem de Anahalt et Magonem" as sons of "Bernardus dux Saxonie" & his wife[579].  2.      
