2 CONT
2 CONT Andrei or Andrew Bogolyubsky succeeded his father Yuri as Grand Duke, reigning over Moscow and the Grand Duchy of Vladimir.  ca. 1157-1174.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Bogolyubsky, Grand Duke of Valdimir defeated and killed the Grand Duke of Kiev.
2 CONT The plundered Kiev, and added that territory to his, and moved the focal point of his kingdom to Moscow, which then became the capital of all Russia.
