2 CONT
2 CONT =Svyatoslav III Igorevich / =
2 CONT
2 CONT Russian:
2 CONT
2 CONT Svyatoslav III [1] Igorevich (1176 – September 1211)[2] was a Rus' prince (a member of the Rurik dynasty).[3] His baptismal name was Adrian.[2] He was prince of Peremyshl (1206, 1208–1209, 1210–1211), and of Volodymyr-Volynskyi (1
2 CONC 206).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His early life===
2 CONT
2 CONT Vladimir was the third son of prince Igor Svyatoslavich of Putivl, by his wife (possibly Evfrosinia Yaroslavna), a daughter of prince Yaroslav Volodimerovich of Halych.[2] Around 1184, Svyatoslav was betrothed to Yaroslava Rurikov
2 CONC na, a daughter of prince Rurik Rostislavich of Belgorod.[2]
2 CONT In 1184, Igor Svyatoslavich dispatched Svyatoslav to escort Vladimir Yaroslavich (Igor Svyatoslavich’s brother-in-law) home when the latter had reconciled with his father (Svyatoslav's maternal grandfather), prince Yaroslav Volodi
2 CONC merovich of Halych.[2] Towards the end of October, 1188, Svyatoslav married his fiancée in Belgorod.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and children[5]===
2 CONT
2 CONT *October, 1188: Yaroslava Yurikovna, a daughter of prince prince Rurik Rustislavich of Belgorod[2] by his wife Anna Yurevna of Turov.[3]
2 CONT # Agafia Svyatoslavna (after 1188 - after August 31, 1247), wife of duke Konrad I of Masovia.[2][3]
