1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Władysław''' (Włodzisław) '''Odonic''' (Plwacz) – '''książę wielkopolski''', 1207-1217 '''książę kaliski''', 1216-1217 w południowo-zachodniej Wielkopolsce (wg innych historyków w całej dzielnicy poznańskiej), o
2 CONC d 1223 książę na Ujściu nad Notecią, od 1225 dodatkowo '''w Nakle''', 1229-1234 w całej Wielkopolsce, 1234-1239 tylko na północ i wschód od rzeki Warty (niektórzy historycy przypuszczają, że na krótko przed śmiercią ponownie usuni
2 CONC ęty do Ujścia i Nakła). [http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw_Odonic Wikipedia PL]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw_Odonic#Marriage_and_Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Władysław Odonic
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to:navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Władysław Odonic's seal, dated from 1231.
2 CONT
2 CONT Władysław (also named Włodzisław) Odonic (nicknamed Plwacz) (Polish: Władysław (Włodzisław) Odonic (Plwacz); b. ca. 1190 - d. 5 June 1239), was a Duke of Kalisz during 1207-1217, Duke of Poznań during 1216-1217, in 1223 ruler over
2 CONC  Ujście, from 1225 ruler over Nakło, Duke of all Greater Poland during 1229-1234, and since 1234 until his death ruler over only the north and east of the Warta river (some historians believed that shortly before his death, he los
2 CONC t Ujście and Nakło).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the eldest son of Odon, Duke of Kalisz, by his wife Viacheslava, daughter of Yaroslav Vladimirovich "Osmomysl", Prince of Halych. Władysław probably received his name after either his paternal uncle Władysław III Spindlesha
2 CONC nks or his ancestor Władysław I Herman.
2 CONT
2 CONT The nickname "Plwacz" (English: the Spitter) was already given to him in the 13th century chronicles. It's unknown if he was named in that way for a disease who affected his throat or because he had bad manners. Another nickname u
2 CONC sed in the contemporary sources was "Odonic", a corruption of his patronymic Odowic ("son of Odon"); here is also unknown why the sources persisted in the erroneus form instead to used the correct.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
