2 CONT https://fi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalvin_kartano
2 CONT Kalvin kartano (vir. Kalvi mõis, saks. Pöddes) on kartano Viru-Nigulan kunnassa Länsi-Virumaan maakunnassa Virossa. Kartano mainitaan ensimmäisen kerran vuonna 1485, kun se oli Lode-suvun hallussa. Vuonna 1512 kartanon sai omistuk
2 CONC sensa Dietrich Kalff, jonka sukunimestä tulee paikan nykyinen nimi. Alun perin kartanon paikalla oli kaksikerroksinen vasallilinnoitus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kalvi Manor (Estonian: Kalvi Manor) Kalvi mõis, Saxon. Pöddes () is a manor in Viru-Nigula Parish, Vest-Viru County, Estonia. The manor is first mentioned in 1485, when it was in the possession of the Lode family. In 1512, the man
2 CONC or was acquired by Dietrich Kalff, whose surname becomes the current name of the place. Initially, on the site of the manor there was a two-story vassal fortress.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Wekebrod's daughter was probably married to Martin Kalff, who owned the lands of Kuusik in the first half of the 15th century. The Kuusik estate and manor are first mentioned in sources in 1467, when male judge Wolmer Treyden an
2 CONC d his two co-judges confirmed the border between the Kuusik Sage and Koikse Koist estates. The lord of Kuusik was then Dietrich Kalff, who inherited the estate from his father Martin Kalff and brother Ludwig Kalff. Kalff had marri
2 CONC ed Elisabeth, the daughter of Dietrich Fahrensbach, the owner of Haimre manor. Dietrich Kalff sold the Kuusik manor Hofes reguliert und verstuisgesetzt in 1467 to the Soye Zoegen family (reports 1479,1497). In 1484, Hermann
2 CONT
2 CONT Jürgen's son Soye pledged the village of Iira Hyr to Jacob Deken's widow Gertrud Wrangell.
2 CONT
