1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXON%20NOBILITY.htm#OdaWerldied1110
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Hermann [III] & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       ODA von Werl ([1050]-13 Jan 1110).  The Annalista Saxo names "comitem Herimannum, pater domne Ode", also naming Oda's husband and (in a later passage) her mother[2984].  The Annales Magdeburgenses the death in 1110 of "O
2 CONC da marchionis…filiastra Ottonis ducis de Northeim"[2985].  The Chronicon Monasterii Rosenfeld seu Hassefeld records the death of “Udo marchio” and in the next line “Id Jan” of “Oda marchionissa”[2986].  m ([1065]) LOTHAR-UDO II Ma
2 CONC rkgraf der Nordmark, Graf von Stade, son of LOTHAR-UDO I Markgraf der Nordmark, Graf von Stade & his wife Adelheid [von Rheinfelden] ([1020/30]-4 May 1082). 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXON%20NOBILITY.htm#LotharUdoIIStadeMgfNordmarkdied1082
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Lothar-Udo [III] & his wife had six children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HEINRICH [III] von Stade ([1065]-27 Jun 1087).  2.         LOTHAR-UDO [IV] von Stade ([1070]-2 Jun 1106).   3.         RUDOLF [I] von Stade (-7 Dec 1124).  4.         SIEGFRIED von Stade (-17 Jun [1110]).  5.         AD
2 CONC ELHEID von Stade (-8 Oct or 14 Nov 1110, bur Reinhardsbrunn).   6.         daughter . 
