1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''MSTISLAV Vladimirovich''', son of VLADIMIR Vsevolodich "Monomakh" Grand Prince of Kiev & his first wife [Gytha of England] 
2 CONT *m secondly (Kiev 1122) '''[LIUBAVA] Dmitrievna''', daughter of DMITRY Zavidich boyar [Passadnik] of Novgorod & his wife --- (-after 1168).
2 CONT *Grand Prince Mstislav II & his second wife had two children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT *12.        ''' IEVFROSINA Mstislavna''' ([1130]-before 1186).  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by a charter dated 1194/95, reciting the consanguinity between Philippe II King of France and his second wife Ingebjörg of De
2 CONC nmark on which their divorce was based, which names “Ingiburgh filia Rizlavi…Ruthenorum Regis et Cristinæ Reginæ…filia…Ingonis Suevorum Regis et Helena Reginæ” as mother of “Waldemarum Regem” and refers to “prædictæ Ingeborgis sor
2 CONC or” as mother of “Belæ Regis Hungariæ” who married “sororem Philippi Regis Francorum”[436].  Baumgarten names the wife of King Géza as the daughter of Prince Mstislav but only cites one secondary source in support[437].  m (1146) 
2 CONC '''GÉZA II King of Hungary''', son of BÉLA II "the Blind" King of Hungary & his wife Jelena of Serbia ([1130]-3 May 1162).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#IevfrosinaMstislavnadiedbefore1186
