2 CONT Euphrosyne of Kiev
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Euphrosyne of Kiev (c. 1130 – c. 1193) was Queen Consort of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Euphrosyne was the first daughter of Grand Prince Mstislav I of Kiev and his second wife, Liubava Dmitrievna.
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT King Géza II of Hungary (1130 – 31 May 1162)
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. King Stephen III of Hungary (1147 – 4 March 1172)
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. King Béla III of Hungary (1148 – 23 April 1196)
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Elisabeth (c. 1149 – after 1189), wife of Duke Frederick of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT -4. Duke Géza (c. 1150 – before 1210)
2 CONT
2 CONT -5. Odola (? – ?), wife of Duke Svatopluk of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT -6. Helena (c. 1158 – 25 May 1199), wife of Duke Leopold V of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT Euphrosyne is an ancestor of Edward III of England and hence the ancestor of all subsequent English and British monarchs. She is also part of a link connecting the line of Harold Godwinson and the modern line of British monarchs.
2 CONT
