2 CONC 32, 1134-1142, 1142-1146.  Prince of Pereyaslavl 1132-1134, 1142.  Prince of Peresopnin 1146-1149.  Prince of Vyshgorod 1149-1151.  He succeeded his brother in 1139 as VIACHESLAV Grand Prince of Kiev, but only ruled 8 days before 
2 CONC ceding the city to Vsevolod Olegovich Prince of Chernigov.  He was restored 1150, but expelled Sep 1150 in favour of his younger brother Iurii.  After Iurii was in his turn expelled Mar 1151, Viacheslav ruled jointly with his neph
2 CONC ew Iziaslav II.  m ---.  The name of Viacheslav´s wife is not known.  Viacheslav & his wife had one child: 
