1 NOTE Sigurd Magnuson, aka the Crusader Sigurd-Jerusalem-farer (the traveler) became sole ruler of Norway after his half-brother Eystein died ca. 1122.  During Sigurd's reign the Swedish Jamtland was made a Norwegian province.  In 1123 
2 CONC he led a crusade, including to Sweden's east coast, where he forcibly baptized a number of local Smalanders. He exacted a tribute from them of 1500 head of cattle.
1 NOTE King of Norway.
1 NOTE     * RESIDENCE: (Først gift med Bladmynja ?)
