2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick (Czech: Bedřich) (died 25 March 1189) was the duke of Olomouc from 1164 and then duke of Bohemia from 1172 to 1173 and again from 1178 to his death. He was the son of King Ladislaus II, who abdicated in 1172 in his favou
2 CONC r. However, he could not hold on to his principality, because he was approved of by neither the national diet nor the emperor, and was deposed in September the year following by the emperor at the Diet of Hermsdorf. The Emperor Fr
2 CONC ederick I, godfather and namesake of Frederick, nominated Oldrich, son of Sobeslav I, but he renounced the throne in favour of Sobeslav II, friend of peasants, but enemy of both nobles and emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick allied with the emperor and defeated Sobeslav at the battles of Lodenice and Prague. The emperor recognised Frederick as an imperial prince, but he also raised the bishop of Prague, Henry Bretislaus, to princely status, 
2 CONC making him a direct vassal of the emperor. He also appointed Conrad Otto margrave over Moravia and thus divided the duchy into three parts dependent on him. When Frederick, who was practically a puppet of the emperor, died, he was
2 CONC  succeeded by Conrad Otto.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his marriage to Elizabeth, daughter of Geza II of Hungary, he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Helena (b.1158), affianced to Peter, son of Manuel I Comnenus, in 1164
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophia (died 25 May 1185), married Albert, Margrave of Meissen
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludmilla (died 14 August 1240), married Adalbert VI, count of Bogen, and then Louis I, Duke of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Vratislaus (d.1180)
2 CONT
2 CONT Olga (fl.c.1163)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (died 28 August 1167)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/bohemia/bohemia2.html#F
2 CONT
