2 CONT a)         BERTHOLD (-Limburg 5/6 Nov 1078, bur Hirsau).  ... He was installed in 1061 as BERTHOLD I "the Bearded" Duke of Carinthia. ... m firstly RICHWARA, daughter of --- (-before [1056]).  ... m secondly ([1056]) BEATRIX de Mo
2 CONC usson, daughter of LOUIS Comte de Mousson & his wife Sophie of Upper Lotharingia  (-26 Oct 1092, bur Toul Cathedral). ... Duke Berthold & his first wife had five children: 
2 CONT *i)          HERMANN ([1045/48]-Cluny 26 Apr 1074).  ... He was installed as Marchese di Verona: ... m JUDITH, daughter of --- (-Salerno 27 Sep 1091, bur Backnang). ... Graf Hermann [I] & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT **(a)       HERMANN [II] (-[7 Oct] [1130], bur Backnang Stiftskirche).  Markgraf 1089.  Markgraf von Limburg 1100.  Graf im Ufgau 1102.  Markgraf von Baden 27 Apr 1112.  -         MARKGRAFEN von BADEN.  
2 CONT *ii)         BERTHOLD ([1050]-12 Apr 1111, bur St Peter in Schwarzwald).  The Genealogia Zaringorum names "Berchtoldus" as son of "Berchtoldus Cum-barba", referring to him first among the brothers, specifying that he was buried at
2 CONC  St Peter in 1111[740].  He was installed in 1092 as BERTHOLD II Duke of Swabia.  He was installed in 1092 as BERTHOLD II Duke of Carinthia, in opposition to Duke Heinrich II [Eppenstein].  Herzog von Zähringen 1100.  -         HE
2 CONC RZOGEN von ZÄHRINGEN.  
2 CONT *iii)        GEBHARD (-12 Nov 1110).  ... Provost at Xanten.  Monk at Hirsau before 1084.  Bishop of Konstanz 1084-1110.  Papal legate in Germany 1099-1107.  
2 CONT *iv.    RICHINZA von Spitzenburg (bur Schaffhausen Allerheiligen).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and two marriages has not yet been identified.  Heiress of Kirchen.  1092/[1110].  m firstly --- von Frickingen . 
2 CONC  m secondly LUDWIG von Sigmaringen [Helfenstein] (-before 1092).  
2 CONT *v)        '''LIUTGARDE (-18 Mar [1119])'''. The Tabula consanguinitatis Friderici I regis et Adelæ reginæ (which provided the basis for their divorce) names "Liutgardim" as daughter of "Bertolfum cum Barba" and mother of "marchio
2 CONC nem Theobaldum"[744].  The Fundatio Monasterii Richenbacensis names "Lukardis" as mother of "marchio Dietpaldus" in connection with the foundation of Reichenbach[745].  The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not
2 CONC  yet been identified.  m firstly DIEPOLD [II] von Giengen Markgraf im Nordgau, son of DIETPOLD [I] Graf [von Cham] [Ratpotonen] & his wife --- (-killed in battle near Wellrichstadt 7 Aug 1078).  m secondly ERNST von Grögling Graf 
2 CONC von Ottenburg, son of [HARTWICH [II] Graf an der unteren Ampar & his wife Avisa ---] (-12 Jan [1096/97]).  
