2 CONT
2 CONT VRATISLAV of Bohemia, son of BŘETISLAV Duke of the Bohemians & his wife Judith von Schweinfurt ([1032]-14 Jan 1093).
2 CONT
2 CONT m thirdly ([1062/63]) SWIĘTOSLAWA [Svatana] of Poland, daughter of KAZIMIERZ I KAROL "Odnowiciel/the Renewer" Prince of Poland & his wife Dobronega Maria Vladimirovna of Kiev ([1048]-1 Sep 1126).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Vratislav II & his third wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.             BOLESLAV (-11 Aug 1091).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.             BOŘIWOJ ([1065]-2 Feb 1124, bur Prague St Veit).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.             VLADISLAV (-12 Apr 1125, bur Prague St Maria).  The Annalista Saxo names (in order) "Bolezlaum, Borivoi, Wladizlaum et Sobezlaum" as the four children of Duke Vratislav by his Polish wife[167].  The Chronica Boemoru
2 CONC m names (in order) "Boleslavum, Borivoy, Wladizlaum, Sobezlavum" as the four children of "Zustavam, Kazimir Poloniorum ducis natam" and "Wratislaus dux"[168].  He succeeded in 1109 as VLADISLAV I Duke of the Bohemians.  The Annale
2 CONC s Gradicenses record that "Borivoy" was expelled in 1116 and replaced by "fratre Wladizlao", but that Borivoy returned in 1117 only to be replaced again in 1120 in favour of "Wladizlaus"[169].  The Chronica Boemorum records the de
2 CONC ath "II Id Apr 1125" of "Wladizlaus", and his burial place[170].  The Annales Gradicenses record the death "1125 II Id Apr" of "dux Wladizlaus pius et misericors ac humilis"[171].  The Cronica Principum Regni Boemiæ records the de
2 CONC ath in 1125 of "Wladislaus…filius Bretislai", adding that he founded "monasterium in Kladruby"[172].  m ([1110]) RICHINZA von Berg, daughter of HEINRICH I Graf von Berg & his wife Adelheid von Mochental (-27 Sep 1125).  Berthold's
2 CONC   Chronicon of Zwiefalten names (in order) "Richinza ductrix Boemiæ, Sophia ductrix Moraviæ, Salome ductrix Poloniæ" as sisters of "Heinricus comes [et] Rapot", specifying in the subsequent paragraph that Richinza was "uxor Vlatiz
2 CONC laus qui et Lauzlan dux Boemiæ"[173].  Duke Vladislav I & his wife had four children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT a)             SVATANA [Liutgarda] (-19 Feb after 1126).  The Chronica Boemorum records the marriage in Jul 1124 of "dux Wladizlaus natam suam primogenitam Suatavam" with "Fridrico"[174].  The primary source which confirms her hus
2 CONC band's identity and parentage has not yet been identified.  m (Jul 1124) as his first wife, FRIEDRICH [IV] Domvogt von Regensburg, son of FRIEDRICH [III] Domvogt von Regensburg & his wife Liutgard --- (-11 Apr 1148, bur Jerusalem)
2 CONC .  He died on the Second Crusade.  
2 CONT
2 CONT b)             VLADISLAV (-18 Jan 1174, bur Strahow).  His parentage is confirmed by the Annales Gradicenses which record that "Wladizlaus filius Sobezlai ducis" was enthroned in Moravia after the expulsion of "Lupoldus dux"[175].
2 CONC   He succeeded in 1140 as VLADISLAV II Duke of Bohemia.  Crowned King of Bohemia at Regensburg 18 Jan 1158.    
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see below, Chapter 3. KINGS of BOHEMIA.  
2 CONT
2 CONT c)             DYPOLD [I] (-14/15 Aug 1167).  The Canonici Wissegradensis Continuatio Cosmæ names "Theobaldum et Henricum" as brothers of Duke Vladislav, recording that they rebelled against their brother in 1142 in Moravia[176]. 
2 CONC  Duke of Moravia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT -        DUKES of MORAVIA.  
2 CONT
2 CONT d)             HEINRICH (-after 1169).  The Canonici Wissegradensis Continuatio Cosmæ names "Theobaldum et Henricum" as brothers of Duke Vladislav, recording that they rebelled against their brother in 1142 in Moravia[177].  m MAR
2 CONC GARETA, daughter of --- (-before 19 Jan 1186).  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  Heinrich & his wife had three children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT i)               ELISABETH .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  Nun.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)             MARGARETA .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not yet been identified.  Nun.  
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)            HEINRICH BŘETISLAV (-15 Jun 1197).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  Archbishop of Prague 1182-1197.  He succeeded in 1193 as HEINRICH BŘETISLAV Duke of Bohemia.  The Cr
2 CONC onica Principum Regni Boemiæ records the death in 1198 of "Bretislaus alias Henricus…qui et Episcopi Pragensis"[178].  
2 CONT
