2 CONC  the church. However, enmity grew between the brothers. It was then that Vratislaus founded the diocese of Olmütz (diocese of Olomouc), under the Archbishopric of Mainz, to counter Otto's authority within his province. Both pope a
2 CONC nd emperor took a hand in refereeing the conflict, which was partially fixed with Henry's appointment of Jaromir as chancellor in 1077. In April 1085, a reichstag convened in Mainz suppressed the Moravian see and, but Vratislaus l
2 CONC ater refounded the see. Jaromir protested in Rome to Pope Urban II, but died in 1090.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sadly for Vratislaus, his last years were occupied by dynastic quarrelling. When his brother Otto died in 1086, he gave Olomouc to his son Boleslaus, which was seen to be an act against the interests of Conrad. Vratislaus raised a
2 CONC n army against Conrad and sent it out under his other son Bretislaus. Instead, this son turned on him. Vratislaus, in keeping with Bohemian custom, designated an heir: Conrad. Thus reconciled with his surviving brother, the two de
2 CONC molished Bretislaus, who fled to Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vratislaus died of a hunting wound on January 14, 1092, after a reign of thirty years. He was buried in St. Peter and Paul′s Church, Vyšehrad.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Vratislaus was married three times. His first wife Maria died during premature childbirth. He married the second time in 1057 to Adelaide, daughter of Andrew I of Hungary, who died in 1061. They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Vratislaus (-1061)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Judith (1056/58-1086), married to Ladislaus I Herman, son of Casimir I of Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ludmila(-after 1100)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bretislaus II of Bohemia (c. 1060–December 22, 1100), Duke of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1062, Vratislaus married a third time to Świętosława of Poland, a daughter of Casimir I of Poland. They had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Boleslaus (-1091)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Borivoj II of Bohemia (c. 1064-February 2, 1124), Duke of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Vladislaus I of Bohemia (-April 12, 1125), Duke of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sobeslav I of Bohemia (-February 14, 1140), Duke of Bohemia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Judith (c. 1066-9 December 1108), married to Wiprecht de Groitzsch
2 CONT
