2 CONT
2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Medlands Project page on Meissen (covering his marriage family):
2 CONT
2 CONT '''KONRAD [I] von Wettin "der Grosse"''', son of THIMO Graf von Brehna & his wife Ida von Northeim ([1097/98]-Kloster Petersberg 5 Feb 1157, bur Kloster Petersberg).  
2 CONT *The Annales Magdeburgenses name "Dedum comitem et Cuonradum marchionem" as the two sons of "Thiemoni comiti de Witin" and his wife Ida von Northeim[323].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Dedonem comitem et Conradum et filiam n
2 CONC omine Machthildem" as the children of "Thiemo comes" & his wife[324].  
2 CONT *'''Graf von Wettin'''
2 CONT *'''Graf von Brehna und Camburg''' before 1116.  
2 CONT *'''Graf von Eilenburg''' 1123.  
2 CONT *Lothar von Süpplingenburg Duke of Saxony appointed Konrad as KONRAD '''Markgraf von Meissen''' in 1123, challenging the rights of Emperor Heinrich V, who had appointed Wiprecht von Groitsch as Markgraf[325].  
2 CONT *'''Markgraf der Ober- und Niederlausitz mit Gau Nisani''' in 1136.  "Conradus…marchio…coniugis nostre…et filiorum nostrorum Ottonis, Heinrici, Theoderici" donated property to Magdeburg Unser Liebe Frau by charter dated [end-May/e
2 CONC arly Jun] 1142[326].  
2 CONT *'''Graf von Groitzsch und Rochlitz''', '''Vogt von Kloster Chemnitz''' 1143.  
2 CONT *'''Vogt of Naumburg cathedral'''.  
2 CONT *'''Founder of St Peter auf dem Lauterberg (Petersberg)'''.  He abdicated and retired to Kloster Petersberg 30 Nov 1156.  
2 CONT *The Annales Erphesfurdenses record the death in 1157 of "Counradus marchio"[327].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni records his death "1157 Non Feb" aged 59, specifying his burial "in medio ecclesie, in dextera ipsius uxor eius [et] 
2 CONC soror eius Machtildis"[328]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before 1119) '''LUITGARD von Elchingen''', daughter of ADALBERT Graf von Elchingen-Ravenstein & his wife Bertha --- (-Kloster Gerbstedt 19 Jun 1145, bur Kloster Gerbstedt).  
2 CONT *The Chronicon Montis Serreni names "Lucardis filia Alberti nobilissimi de Suevia" as wife of "Conradus comes de Witin"[329].  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Lucardem filiam cuiusdam nobilissimi de Suevia nomine Alberti" as wi
2 CONC fe of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientalius marchio [filius Thiemonis]"[330].  The Annales Magdaburgenses record the death in 1145 of "Luthgart marchionissa"[331]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Markgraf Konrad [I] & his wife had [twelve] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HEINRICH (-young).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Heinricum…Othonem Misnensem marchionem, Tidericum Orientalem marchionem, Dedonem comitem de Rochelitz, Heinricum comitem de Witin, Fridericum comitem de Brene" as sons of "Conradus Mi
2 CONC snensis et Orientalius marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife, specifying that Heinrich died in boyhood[332]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         OTTO ([1125]-18 Feb 1190, bur Kloster Altzelle).  
2 CONT *The Chronicon Montis Serreni names (in order) brothers "Othonis Misniensis marchionis, Tiderici Orientalis marchionis, Heinrici comitis de Witin, Dedonis comitis de Rochelez, Friderici comitis de Brene"[333].  
2 CONT *He succeeded in 1156 as '''OTTO "der Reiche" Markgraf von Meissen, zu Colditz und Lausick'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         ODA (-2 Jun <nowiki>----</nowiki>).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Odam et Bertam abbatissam Gerbestadensem, Agnetam Quidelingenburgensem abbatissam, quarta…Gerdrudis…quinta Adela…sexta Sophia" as the six daughters of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientali
2 CONC us marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[334].  
2 CONT *'''Abbess of Gerbstedt''' 1137. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         BERTA .  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Odam et Bertam abbatissam Gerbestadensem, Agnetam Quidelingenburgensem abbatissam, quarta…Gerdrudis…quinta Adela…sexta Sophia" as the six daughters of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientali
2 CONC us marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[335].  
2 CONT *'''Abbess of Gerbstedt''' 1190. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         DIETRICH (-Petersberg 9 Feb 1185, bur Petersberg).  
2 CONT *The Chronicon Montis Serreni names (in order) brothers "Othonis Misniensis marchionis, Tiderici Orientalis marchionis, Heinrici comitis de Witin, Dedonis comitis de Rochelez, Friderici comitis de Brene"[336].  "Conradus…marchio…c
2 CONC oniugis nostre…et filiorum nostrorum Ottonis, Heinrici, Theoderici" donated property to Magdeburg Unser Liebe Frau by charter dated [end-May/early Jun] 1142[337].  
2 CONT *'''Markgraf der Niederlausitz und Graf von Eilenburg''' 1156.  The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Heinricum…Othonem Misnensem marchionem, Tidericum Orientalem marchionem, Dedonem comitem de Rochelitz, Heinricum comitem
2 CONC  de Witin, Fridericum comitem de Brene" as sons of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientalius marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[338].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni records the death "1184 V Id Feb" of "Tidericus Orientalis marchio, f
2 CONC ilius Conradi marchione defuncti"[339].  The Genealogica Wettinensis records the death in 1184 of "Tidericus Orientalis marchio"[340].  
2 CONT *m ([1142]) DOBRONEGA LUDGARDA of Poland, daughter of BOLESŁAW III "Krzywousty/Wrymouth" Prince of Poland & his second wife Salome von Berg-Schelklingen (before 1129-after 26 Oct 1147).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "sororem 
2 CONC Meseconis ducis Polonie, Dobernegam…que etiam Lukardis dicta est" as wife of "Tidericus Orientalis marchio"[341].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names "soror…Mesoconis ducis Polonie Dobergana que et Lucardis vocabatur" as the wife 
2 CONC of "Tidericus Orientalis marchio, filius Conradi marchione defuncti"[342].  
2 CONT *Mistress (1): (after Oct 1147) KUNIGUNDE from Bavaria, widow of BERNHARD Graf von Plötzkau, daughter of --- (-after 1185).  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names "Conigundam comitissam viduam Bernhardi de Plozke" as "aliam [uxorem]"
2 CONC  of "Tidericus Orientalis marchio, filius Conradi marchione defuncti"[343].  
2 CONT *Markgraf Dietrich & his wife had two children: Konrad (killed in a tournament 17 February 1175) and Gertrud, nun at Gerbstedt.
2 CONT *Markgraf Dietrich had one illegitimate child by Mistress (1): Dietrich, Bishop of Merseburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         [GERTRUD .  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Odam et Bertam abbatissam Gerbestadensem, Agnetam Quidelingenburgensem abbatissam, quarta…Gerdrudis…quinta Adela…sexta Sophia" as the six daughters of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientali
2 CONC us marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife, specifying that Gertrud married "palatino Reni" and founded "ecclesiam in honore beati Theodori Bavenberg" after her husband died[349].  However, this supposed parentage of the wife of Pf
2 CONC alzgraf Hermann appears disproved by the charter dated 1138 under which "Heremannus palatinus comes de Stahelekke" assumed the Vogtei of Kloster Lorch, at the request of "domne Gertrudis…contoralis nostre fratrisque sui Friderici…
2 CONC ducis Swevie"[350].  
2 CONT *m HERMANN von Stahleck Graf von Stahleck, son of GOSWIN Graf von Stahleck & his wife Luitgard von Heimbach (-Ebrach 2 Oct 1156, bur Ebrach, transferred to Bildhausen).  He was installed in [1138] as HERMANN III Pfalzgraf von Loth
2 CONC ringen by his brother-in-law Konrad III King of Germany, resigned in 1155.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.         ADELHEID (-after 6 Dec 1172).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Odam et Bertam abbatissam Gerbestadensem, Agnetam Quidelingenburgensem abbatissam, quarta…Gerdrudis…quinta Adela…sexta Sophia" as the six daughters of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientali
2 CONC us marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife, specifying that Adela married firstly "regi Danorum Suenoni" and secondly "Albertus comes Alberti marchionis filius"[351].  A 13th century genealogy names "Adelam" as daughter of "marchio
2 CONC  Conradus" and her first husband as "regi Dacie" and her second "de Saxonia"[352].  
2 CONT *m firstly ([1152], repudiated 1153) SVEND III Erikssen "Grade" King of Denmark, son of ERIK II "Emun" King of Denmark & his wife Malmfred Mstislavna of Kiev (-murdered 23 Oct 1157).  
2 CONT *m secondly (end 1157) ALBRECHT Graf von Ballenstedt, son of ALBRECHT "der Bär" Markgraf von Brandenburg [Ballenstedt] & his wife Sophie von Winzenburg ([1131/40]-after 6 Dec 1172). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.         HEINRICH [I] (before 27 Feb 1142-30 Aug 1181, bur Petersberg).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Heinricum…Othonem Misnensem marchionem, Tidericum Orientalem marchionem, Dedonem comitem de Rochelitz, Heinricum comitem de Witin, Fridericum comitem de Brene" as sons of "Conradus Mi
2 CONC snensis et Orientalius marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[353].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names (in order) brothers "Othonis Misniensis marchionis, Tiderici Orientalis marchionis, Heinrici comitis de Witin, Dedonis comitis
2 CONC  de Rochelez, Friderici comitis de Brene"[354].  "Conradus…marchio…coniugis nostre…et filiorum nostrorum Ottonis, Heinrici, Theoderici" donated property to Magdeburg Unser Liebe Frau by charter dated [end-May/early Jun] 1142[355].
2 CONC
2 CONT *'''Graf von Wettin''' 1156.  The Genealogica Wettinensis records the death in 1181 of "Heinricum comes senior de Witin"[356].  
2 CONT *m as her first husband, SOPHIE, daughter of --- (-1189, bur Reinhardsbrunn).  The Genealogica Wettinensis names "Sophiam filiam cuiusdam nobilis de Austria" as wife of "Heinricus comes de Witin", specifying that she married secon
2 CONC dly "Hermannus tunc comes palatinus Saxonie, postmodem etiam comes provincialis Thuringie"[357].  She married secondly ([1182]) as his first wife, Hermann von Thüringen Pfalzgraf of Saxony, who succeeded in 1190 as Hermann I Landg
2 CONC raf of Thuringia.  
2 CONT *Graf Heinrich [I] & his wife had four children: Heinrich II (d. 28 December 1187), Konrad (d.y.), Ulrich (d. 28 September 1206), and Sophie (d. 1195)
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.         DEDO [V] "der Feiste" (-16 Aug 1190, bur Kloster Zschillen).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Heinricum…Othonem Misnensem marchionem, Tidericum Orientalem marchionem, Dedonem comitem de Rochelitz, Heinricum comitem de Witin, Fridericum comitem de Brene" as sons of "Conradus Mi
2 CONC snensis et Orientalius marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[370].  
2 CONT *'''Graf von Groitzsch''' 1144. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 10.      AGNES (-21 Jan 1203, bur Quedlinburg).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Odam et Bertam abbatissam Gerbestadensem, Agnetam Quidelingenburgensem abbatissam, quarta…Gerdrudis…quinta Adela…sexta Sophia" as the six daughters of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientali
2 CONC us marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[371].  
2 CONT *The Annales Pegavienses name "Agnes soror marchionis Ottonis de Misna" when recording her appointment as '''Abbess of Quedlinburg''' in 1184[372].  
2 CONT *'''Nun at Gerbstedt'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.      SOPHIE (-16 Apr [after 1190]).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Odam et Bertam abbatissam Gerbestadensem, Agnetam Quidelingenburgensem abbatissam, quarta…Gerdrudis…quinta Adela…sexta Sophia" as the six daughters of "Conradus Misnensis et Orientali
2 CONC us marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife, naming "Gebehardo comiti de Bavaria, filio sororis Luderi imperatoris" as husband of Sophie[373].  The necrology of Michaelbeuern records the death "XVI Kal May" of "Sophia com de Burchus
2 CONC en"[374].  
2 CONT *m ([1144]) GEBHARD [I] Graf von Burghausen, son of SIEGHARD [X] Graf von Tengling [Sieghardinger] & his wife Ida von Süpplingenburg (-4 Dec [1163], bur Michaelsbeuern). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 12.      FRIEDRICH [I] ([27 Feb 1142/19 May 1145]-4 Jan 1191, bur Petersberg).  
2 CONT *The Genealogica Wettinensis names (in order) "Heinricum…Othonem Misnensem marchionem, Tidericum Orientalem marchionem, Dedonem comitem de Rochelitz, Heinricum comitem de Witin, Fridericum comitem de Brene" as sons of "Conradus Mi
2 CONC snensis et Orientalius marchio [filius Thiemonis]" & his wife[375].  The Chronicon Montis Serreni names (in order) brothers "Othonis Misniensis marchionis, Tiderici Orientalis marchionis, Heinrici comitis de Witin, Dedonis comitis
2 CONC  de Rochelez, Friderici comitis de Brene"[376].  
2 CONT *'''Graf von Brehna''' 1156.
2 CONT
