1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#IelisavetaRostislavnadied12961298 Medlands] she is called Anna Rostislavna
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/RUSSIA,%20Rurik.htm#IelisavetaRostislavnadied12961298
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         ANNA Rostislavna ([after 1243]-[1296/98]).  Her parentage and first marriage are indicated by Georgius Akropolites who names "Rosum Urum…Ungariæ regis generum" as father-in-law of "Bulgarorum…princeps"[341].  Her first 
2 CONC marriage was arranged to confirm the alliance between Bulgaria and Hungary in 1255[342].  After the death of her first husband, his successor forcibly married her.  Georgius Akropolites records that "consobrino suo Callimano" marr
2 CONC ied "Bulgarorum princeps…Michael…uxore" after killing her first husband[343].  After the latter's death shortly after, she was handed back to her father after he invaded Bulgaria[344].  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[345], t
2 CONC he wife of Moys de Dáró was the daughter of András of Hungary & his wife Ielena Mstislavna of Galich.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ([1255]) MIHAIL II ASEN Tsar of the Bulgarians, son of IVAN ASEN II Tsar of the Bulgarians & his third wife Eirene Komnene Angelina of Epirus ([1238]-murdered 1257).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (1257) KOLOMAN II Tsar of the Bulgarians, son of ALEXANDER of Bulgaria, sébastokrator & his wife --- of Serbia (-murdered 1258).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m'''[346] thirdly (May 1260) MOYS de Dáró, Judge of the Kumans, Palatine of Hungary, Gespan of Sopron, son of --- (-end 1280). 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/hung/daroi.html
