2 CONT Stub icon 	This biography of a member of a European royal house is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Mestwin I, Duke of Pomerania
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Hermann Hahn: Mestwin I of Pomerania, about 1620
2 CONT
2 CONT  Seal of Mestvinus dux Pomeraniae Mestwin I [1][2] (Polish: Mściwój I gdański or Mszczuj I; born c. 1160, died 1/2 May 1219 or 1220) was regent (a "namiestnik" or starosta) of Pomerelia (princeps in Danzk, i.e. prince of Gdansk/Da
2 CONC nzig)[3] from about 1205 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mestwin was a member of the Samborides dynasty, the son of Duke Sobiesław of Gdańsk and younger brother of Sambor I, whom he succeeded in Pomerelia by appointment of the Polish High Duke Władysław III Spindleshanks. In the tables 
2 CONC of Oliwa Abbey, he is recorded as pacificus ("the Peaceful").
2 CONT
2 CONT As Mestwin I, dei gracia princeps in Gdanzk,[4] he had founded a convent of nuns (probably the Premonstratensian abbey of Żukowo), the castellany of Białogarda at the border with the Pomeranian Lands of Schlawe and Stolp on the Łe
2 CONC ba river, and several villages between the rivers Radunia and Słupia. After King Valdemar II of Denmark had conquered the southern coast of the Baltic Sea with Gdanzk during a crusade against the Old Prussians, Duke Mestwin in 121
2 CONC 0 had to accept Danish overlordship, but was able to free himself again the next year.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Swinisława (d. 1240), maybe a daughter of Polish High Duke Mieszko III the Old, formerly also referred to as a daughter of Duke Ratibor I of Pomerania. They had eight children:[5] 1.Mirosława, married Bogislaw II
2 CONC , Duke of Pomerania at Stettin 2.Swietopelk II, Duke of Pomerania, succeeded his father as Duke of Pomerelia, from 1227 of Pomerelia-Gdańsk 3.Hedwig (Jadwiga), married Duke Władysław Odonic of Greater Poland 4.Witosława, prioress 
2 CONC of Żukowo Abbey 5.Warcisław, Duke at Świecie from 1227 6.Sambor II, Duke at Lubiszewo from 1233 7.Ratibor, Duke at Białogard from 1233 8.Milosława, nun at Żukowo Abbey
2 CONT
2 CONT See also [edit] List of Pomeranian duchies and dukes Pomerania during the High Middle Ages
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mestwin_I,_Duke_of_Pomerania
