1 OCCU Khan of the Kumans
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aëpa II Ocenevich was the Khan of the Cumans, a Turkic nomadic tribe that lived in the steppes of Central Asia during the early Middle Ages. The Cumans also lived in modern-day Ukraine and Russia, and as far east a
2 CONC s Kazakhstan. They were also known as the Polovtsians or Folban. 
2 CONT Aëpa II's daughter, Aëpovna, Princess of the Cumans, had a daughter named Maria Yuryevna with Yuri I Vladimirovich Dolgoruky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aëpa II, Khan of the Kumans is our 29th great grandfather.
2 CONT Janet Milburn
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT THE THREE DAUGHTERS OF KHAN AEPA
2 CONT
2 CONT The website "Our Royal, Titled, Noble, and Commoner Ancestors" (citing "Europaische Stammtafela, Vol. II" by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenberg) develops that Khan Aepa was the father of three daughters by unknown mothers and / or co
2 CONC ncubines --
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.) "Miss von Polowcen", who married Vladimir II of Kiev
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.) "Miss Polowcen", who married Svyatoslav II Olgovich, Duke of Chernigov (circa 1090 - 1164)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.)  Anna Aepovna (born circa 1092), who married Yuri I "Dolgoruki" 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/110326636/person/120101114407 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 23 2017, 12:50:28 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/110326636/person/120101114407/facts Ancestry Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 23 2017, 12:50:48 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Despite the weakening  of Kumans and the rigid control over them on the part of the Rus Princes, Vladimir Monomah supported his prestige in the steppes not only by  military actions, but also by numerous peace treaties he conclude
2 CONC d with heads of separate hordes, thus also breaking tribal unity. So, in January 1107 Vladimir, Davyd and Oleg went to the steppe to the Ayapa (Ayubay, a son of Azan, son of Ishim, from the ruling clan of the Kipchak horde) and an
2 CONC other Ayapa  pasturelands. They concluded peace with Kumans, and Vladimir married his son George (future Üry/Yury (his Türkic name was Djurgi) Dolgoruky (Long Limbs)) to a daughter of Epiop (just another distortion of the same nam
2 CONC e Ayubay, she was a first cousin of Sharukan and a granddaughter of Kipchak great Khan Ishim), and Oleg (of Karajar/Chernihiv, his Türkic name was Yolyg, meaning "divinator" ("prophet") took for his son Akaepida daughter of Yan's 
2 CONC grandson. Later, in the 1117 Vladimir concluded one more important dynastic marriage, marrying his son Andrey to a granddaughter of Tugorkan. With these marriages he substantially secured the border of the Pereyaslavl princedom.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://s155239215.onlinehome.us/turkic/26Kipchaks/Pletneva/KipchaksPletneva2En.htm
