1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaac Komnenos
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Komnenos was married to Eirene, possibly a Kievan princess. He may also have married Kata of Georgia, daughter of David IV of Georgia and Rusudan of Armenia. By his first marriage, he had:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Comnenus called Tzelepes (i.e., Çelebi), who became a Muslim.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andronikos I Komnenos, emperor 1183–1185.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Komnene, who married before 1166 Joseph Bryennios.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Komnene, who married John Arbantenos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eudokia Komnene, who probably married Constantine Palaiologos.
2 CONT
2 CONT Helena Komnene (d. 1183), who probably married Yury Dolgoruky of Kiev.
