1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Diedrich von Tiesenhausen auf Kongota, auf Koskullshof und Stumpen (seit 20.10.1598), Livland. (GHdA 27, Freiherren A IV, p. 445).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Tiesenhausen family originates from Tiesenhusen, situated in Northern Germany between Nienburg and Holtorf in the lower Weser region ("Unterweser"). They were knights of the counts Wölpe. The Tiesenhausen first mentioned is En
2 CONC gelbertus de Tysenhusen, who sailed together Albert von Buxhövede to Livland (today Latvia). Buxhövede was not only Engelbertus brother-in-law, but also later became the first bishop of Riga. There, the family soon rose to influen
2 CONC ce and prosperity, not least through the policy that only allowed the sale of land within the family. It is presumed, but not proven, that Diedrich is a descendant of Engelbertus.
