2 CONT Heinrich I (died 1183) was the first to take the name of Hohenlohe, and in 1230 his grandsons, Gottfried and Conrad, supporters of Emperor Frederick II, founded the lines of Hohenlohe-Hohenlohe and Hohenlohe-Brauneck, names taken 
2 CONC from their respective castles. The latter became extinct in 1390, its lands passing later to Brandenburg, while the former was divided into several branches
