1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gertrude_of_Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gertrude of Bavaria''', also called '''Gertrude of Saxony''' (Danish and German: ''Gertrud''; 1152/55–1197), was Duchess of Swabia as the spouse of Duke Frederick IV, and Queen of Denmark as the spouse of King Canute VI.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude was born to Henry the Lion of Bavaria and Saxony and Clementia of Zähringen in either 1152 or 1155.[1] She was married to Frederick IV, Duke of Swabia, in 1166, and became a widow in 1167. In 1171, she was engaged and in 
2 CONC February 1177 married to Canute of Denmark in Lund.[2] The couple lived the first years in Skåne.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 12 May 1182, they became king and queen. She did not have any children. During her second marriage, she chose to live in chastity and celibacy with her husband. Chronicler Arnold of Lübeck remarked of their marriage that her sp
2 CONC ouse was: "The most chaste one, living thus his days with his chaste spouse" in eternal chastity.
