2 CONT ====FMG: [https://www.geni.com/people/Prince-Otto-of-Austria-bishop-of-Freising/6000000003097932831 Austria]
2 CONT * 6. '''OTTO''' (1112-Morimond 22 Sep 1158, bur Morimond). The ''Continuatio Claustroneoburgensis'' names "Otto" as fifth son of "''Liupoldus marchio Austrie''" and "''Agnetem imperatoris Heinrici IV filiam''"[194]. 
2 CONT * Provost at Klosterneuburg in [1126]. 
2 CONT * He studied in France under Hugues de Saint-Victor.  
2 CONT * In 1133, he became a monk with the Cistercian Order at Morimond, diocese of Langres.  
2 CONT * Abbot of Morimond.  
2 CONT * He was elected Bishop of Freising in 1138.  
2 CONT * He took part in the Second Crusade in 1147.  
2 CONT * He wrote the work of historical theology ''Chronica sive Historia de duabus civitatibus'' between 1143 and 1146.  
2 CONT * Between 1157 and 1158, he wrote the first two books of the Gesta Friderici, dealing with the history of the kings of Germany since Heinrich IV[195].  
2 CONT * The ''Continuatio Claustroneoburgensis'' records the death in 1158 of "''Otto Frisingensis episcopus, Liupoldi pii marchionis filius''"[196].  
2 CONT * The necrology of Kloster Neuburg records the death "''X Kal Sep''" of "''Otto Liupoldi marchionis Austrie fil, Frisingensis eps''"[197].   
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otto_of_Freising
