1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bertha,_Duchess_of_Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha of Lorraine (or Bertha of Swabia) (b.c. 1123/30 – d. 1194/5) was duchess of Lorraine (c.1138-1176) by marriage to Matthias I duke of Lorraine. She had a contested regency in the beginning of her son's rule, but was deposed 
2 CONC from her position because her son was an adult.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT Bertha (sometimes called Judith) was the daughter of Frederick II, Duke of Swabia and Judith of Bavaria (1103- 22 February 1131), daughter of Henry IX, Duke of Bavaria.[1] Through her father, Bertha was a member of the Hohenstaufe
2 CONC n dynasty: her paternal uncle was king Conrad III and her brother was the future emperor Frederick Barbarossa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha married Matthias of Lorraine c.1138.[2] Bertha frequently issued charters alongside her husband.[3] She used at least two different types of seal to authenticate her documents, on which she was riding astride on horseback, 
2 CONC which was a highly unusual image for a medieval noblewoman to use.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Matthias in 1176, he was succeeded by his son with Bertha, Simon, as duke of Lorraine. Due to the weak health of her son, Bertha took power as regent and issued documents which she co-signed with her son.[5] Bec
2 CONC ause her son was an adult, her regency was considered illegal and widely opposed by the nobility, and resulted in her excommunication. She was forced to resign from her political position and perform penitence before the Bishop pf
2 CONC  Metz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT With Matthias I, Bertha had several children, including:[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon (died 1205), his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT Frederick (died 1206), count of Bitche and his nephew's successor
2 CONT Judith (died 1173), married Stephen II of Auxonne (1170)
2 CONT Alice (died 1200), married Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT Theoderic (died 1181), bishop of Metz (1174–1179)
2 CONT Matthias (died 1208), count of Toul
2 CONT Unnamed daughter who died young
2 CONT References
2 CONT  Brooke, Europe in the Central Middle Ages, p. 438.
2 CONT  Jasperse, ‘Manly Minds,’ p. 311.
2 CONT  Jasperse, 'To Have and to Hold'.
2 CONT  Jasperse, ‘Manly minds,’ pp. 311-5.
2 CONT  Jasperse, 'To Have and to Hold,'pp. 94-5.
2 CONT  Poull, La maison ducale de Lorraine, pp. 37-39.
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT C. Brooke, Europe in the Central Middle Ages (Routledge, 2014).
2 CONT J. Jasperse, ‘To Have and to Hold: Coins and Seals as Evidence for Motherly Authority,' In C. Fleiner and E. Woodacre, (eds): Royal Mothers and Their Ruling Children. Wielding Political Authority from Antiquity to the Early Modern
2 CONC  Era (Basingstoke, Palgrave Macmillan, 2015), pp. 83–104.
2 CONT J. Jasperse, ‘Manly Minds in Female Bodies: Three Women and their Power through Coins and Seals’, Arenal: Revista de historia de las mujeres 25:2 (2018), 295-321.
2 CONT G. Poull, La maison ducale de Lorraine devenue la maison impériale et royale d’Autriche, de Hongrie et de Bohême (Nancy, Presses universitaires de Nancy, 1991).
2 CONT Jacqueline Carolus-Curien Pauvres duchesses, l'envers du décor à la cour de Lorraine. Éditions Serpenoise, Metz, 2007. (ISBN 978-2-87692-715-5).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias I, Duke of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Judith (sometimes called Bertha), daughter of Frederick II, Duke of Swabia, and therefore niece of the Hohenstaufen king Conrad III and sister of Frederick Barbarossa, future emperor. By his Hohenstaufen marriage (1138)
2 CONC , he had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon (d.1205), his successor in Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick (d.1206), count of Bitche and his nephew's successor
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith (d.1173), married Stephen II, count of Auxonne (1170)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice (d.1200), married Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Thierry (d.1181), bishop of Metz (1174-1179)
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthias (d.1208), count of Toul
2 CONT
2 CONT Unnamed daughter who died young
2 CONT
