2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         SIGEBERT [I] (-1105 or after). ... Graf im Saargau.  m ---.  The name of Sigebert's wife is not known.  Graf Sigebert [I] & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT **a)         SIGEBERT [II] (-1130 or after). ... Graf von Elsass.  Graf von Hohenburg.  Vogt von Rosheim.    -        GRAFEN von WERD, GRAFEN von RIXINGEN[673]. 
2 CONT **b)         FRIEDRICH [I] (-before 1135).  ... Graf von Saarbrücken.  ... m as her second husband, GISELA, widow of --- [von Tecklenburg], daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her first marriage has not yet been id
2 CONC entified.  According to Europäische Stammtafeln[675], she may have been Gisela de Lorraine, daughter of Thierry II Duke of Lorraine & his second wife Gertrude de Flandre.  ... Graf Friedrich [I] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT ***i)          SIMON [I] (-1183 or after).  Archbishop of Trier confirmed the donation to Kloster Wadegozingen made by "domina Gisela comitis Friderici de Sarbrucken vidua…cum filio suo Simone" by charter dated 1135[677].  Graf vo
2 CONC n Saarbrücken 1139. -         see below. ►
2 CONT ***ii)         ADALBERT (-Erfurt 17 Jul 1141, bur Mainz Cathedral). ...  Archbishop of Mainz 1138. 
2 CONT ***iii)        '''AGNES (-bur Abtei Walburg)'''. ... m ([1132/33]) as his second wife, FRIEDRICH II “der Einäugige” Duke of Swabia, son of FRIEDRICH I Duke of Swabia [Staufen] & his wife Agnes of Germany (1090-Alzey 4 or 6 Apr 114
2 CONC 7, bur Walburg Abbey). 
2 CONT **c)         ADALBERT (-23 Jun 1137).  ... Archbishop of Mainz 1111. 
2 CONT **d)         BRUNO (-19 Oct 1123, bur Limburg an der Hardt). ... Abbot of Lorsch.  Bishop of Speyer 1107. 
2 CONT *2.         WINITHER (-after 1088). ... Abbot of Hornbach 1072.  Abbot of Lorsch 1077.  Elekt von Worms 1085.  Monk at Hirsau 1088. 
