2 CONT * Married:  (1101) as her first husband,''' MARGRETA "Fredkulla/peace-bringing woman" of Sweden,'daughter of INGE I Stenkilsson King of Sweden (-4 Nov [1130], bur Roskilde).'''  Snorre records that the marriage of "King Inge's dau
2 CONC ghter Margaret" and King Magnus was agreed at "Konghelle on the Gaut river" under the agreement which settled disputes between the kings of Norway, Denmark and Sweden. According to Saxo, her first marriage took place after the pea
2 CONC ce meeting between the three Scandinavian kings at Gotaalv in 1101, hence her nickname.  She married secondly ([1105]) Niels King of Denmark.  Snorre names "Queen Margaret, a daughter of King Inge, who had before been married to K
2 CONC ing Magnus Barefoot" as the wife of "the Danish king Nikolas, a son of Svein Ulfson".
