2 CONT * Mistress (1): Unknown,  Snorre records that King Magnus's son Eystein "was of a mean mother."
2 CONT * Mistress (2): '''THORA,'''  Snorre names Thora as the mother of King Magnus's son Sigurd. 
2 CONT * Mistress (3): '''SIGRID Saxesdatter,'''  Snorre names "Sigrid, a daughter of Saxe of Vik…a respectable man in the Trondheim country" as the mother of King Magnus's son Olav[379].  Morkinskinna names “Sigrídr, the daughter of Sax
2 CONC i from Vik…sister of Kári from Austrátt…called Kári King´s brother” as mother of King Sigurd´s son King Olav.
2 CONT * Mistress (4): Unknown.  The name of King Magnus's fourth mistress is not known. 
2 CONT * Mistress (5):  Unknown Irish woman.  Snorre records that the mother of "Gillikrist…Harald" supported her son's claim to be the son of King Magnus.
2 CONT * Mistress (6):  Snorre names. '''Thora,''' a daughter of Saxe of Vik, a sister of Sigrid who was mother of King Olaf Magnsuson and of Kare the king's brother who married Borghild, a daughter of Dag Eilifson" as the mother of "Sig
2 CONC urd." Morkinskinna records that “Thora” daughter of “Saxi in Vik” was the mother of “Sigurdr…slembidjákn” who was “later alleged to be Magnus´s son.”
