2 CONT >>>>* i)          '''OLAV Ugjäve''' (-Aalborg 1173).  Snorre names "Olaf, a son of Gudbrand Skafhaug and Maria, a daughter of King Eystein Magnuson", recording that he was brought up "in the house of Sigurd Agnhot in the Uplands" 
2 CONC and gathered troops and was chosen king by many Upland people[393].  He was a contender for the throne in 1170.
