2 CONT Erik I 'the Evergood' Svendsson, King of Denmark was the son of Svend II Estrithson, King of Denmark and Gunhilda Sweynsdottir.1,2 He married Bothilde Thorgautsdottir, daughter of Thorgaut Ulvson. He died on 10 July 1103 at Cyprus
2 CONC . He succeeded to the title of King Erik I of Denmark in 1095.2 Children of Erik I 'the Evergood' Svendsson, King of Denmark and Bothilde Thorgautsdottir Erik II 'the Memorable' Eriksson, King of Denmark+1 d. 18 Sep 1137 Harald Ke
2 CONC sia Eriksson, Prince of Denmark d. 1135 Ragnhild Eriksdottir+ Knut Lavard Eriksson, Duke of South Jutland+ b. 1096, d. 1131 Citations [S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxf
2 CONC ordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 149. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World. [S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.
