1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Þóra (Tora) Magnusdóttir''' (mor till Jón Loftsson í Odda. Han uppfostrade Snorri Sturluson och var far till Páll Jónsson biskop i Skálholt.). Det er ingen kilder til som viser at hun har fået flere børn end Jon
2 CONC  Loftsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT NB! Tora var IKKE mor til Gunbjörn Ormsson Drotning eller Jon Ormsson Drotning !!!! [sign: Anna Petursdottir]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16. Konung Magnus giftermål.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Konung Magnus äktade drottning Margareta. Hon sändes västerut från Svithiod till Norge med ett präktigt följe. Konung Magnus hade förut några barn, vilkas namn äro kända. Östen hette hans äldste son; hans moder var av ringa härkom
2 CONC st. Den andre hette Sigurd; han var ett år yngre; hans moder hette Thora. Olav hette den tredje; han var mycket yngre än de båda andra. Olavs moder var Sigrid, dotter till en framstående man i Trondheim, Saxe i Vik; hon var konung
2 CONC ens frilla eft. 1090. 
2 CONT
2 CONT #https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tora_Magnusdatter
2 CONT #http://heimskringla.no/wiki/Konung_Magnus_barfots_historia
2 CONT #https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnus_Berrf%C3%B8tt
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Þóra Magnúsdóttir (born 1100 in Norway) was a daughter of Magnus III of Norway a direct descendant of Harald Fairhair the first Norwegian King. The Fairhair dynasty is traditionally regarded as the first royal dynasty of the unite
2 CONC d Norway, a branch of the Ynglings.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%9E%C3%B3ra_Magn%C3%BAsd%C3%B3ttir
2 CONT
2 CONT Þóra Magnusdóttir married an Icelander and moved to Iceland. Her husband was a powerful Icelandic chieftain Loftur Sæmundsson son of Sæmundur fróði Sigfússon. Their son was Jón Loftsson. A direct descendant of Loftur and Þóra was 
2 CONC Þuríður Sturludóttir (born 1228) who married Hrafn Oddsson (born 1225) a direct descendant of Sakallagrímur Kveldúlfsson (Skalla-Grímr) father of skald and viking Egill Skallagrímsson. In their son Jón korpur Hrafnsson (born 1255)
2 CONC  the two warring clans of Haraldur hárfagri and Skallagímur Kveldúlfsson were genetically united in Iceland.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Genealogy
