1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#ErnstGroglingdied1096B
2 CONT
2 CONT ERNST, son of [HARTWICH [II] Graf an der unteren Ampar & his wife Avisa ---] (-12 Nov [1096/97]).  Wegener highlights the absence of proof that Ernst was the son of Hartwig [II], but emphasises that this looks likely both because 
2 CONC of the onomastics and the connection with Eichstädt[1220].  Graf 1070.  Vogt zu Eichstätt 1085.  Graf von Grögling 1096.  Graf von Ottenburg.  The Liber Oblagiorum of Freising Cathedral records the death "II Id Nov" of "Ernest com
2 CONC ", and his donation of "Druchtering"[1221]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (after Aug 1078) as her second husband, LIUTGARD von Zähringen, widow of DIEPOLD [II] von Giengen Markgraf im Nordgau, daughter of BERTHOLD I Duke of Carinthia, Markgraf of Verona & his first wife Richwara of Swabia (-18 M
2 CONC ar [1119]).  Wegener refers to the "tabula consanguinitatis" of Wibald von Corvey which names Liutgard as the daughter of "Bertolfus cum Barba" and mother of "marchio Theobaldus"[1222].  The Fundatio Monasterii Richenbacensis name
2 CONC s "Lukardis" as mother of "marchio Dietpaldus" in connection with the foundation of Reichenbach[1223].  The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not yet been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Graf Ernst & his wife had four children: 
