1 OCCU war durch Geburt eine polnische Prinzessin und durch Heirat Markgräfin auf dem Nordgau und von Nabburg, Vohburg an der Donau und Cham.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She and https://www.geni.com/people/NN/6000000003087188060?through=6000000003087080306 are not the same person.
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT MedLands & Wikipedia [de][eng] identify she 4th daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw-I-Herman-Duke-of-Poland/6000000003087080306, (sister of the aforementioned) Poles say no.
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelajda_von_Polen ''(she)''
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw_I_Herman ''(her father and sisters)''
2 CONT
2 CONT #[https://www.geni.com/people/Judith-Maria-of-Kiev/6000000010107772824 Sophia] (b. c. 1089 – d. bef. 12 May 1112), married bef. 1108 to [https://www.geni.com/people/Yaroslav-of-Volynya/6000000006727873998 Yaroslav Sviatopolkovich,
2 CONC  Prince of Volhynia], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Grand-Prince-of-Kiev-Sviatopolk-II/6000000003494757665?through=6000000006727873998 Sviatopolk II of Kiev].
2 CONT #[https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-I-Abbess-of-Quedlinburg/367922923820005107 Agnes] (b. c. 1090 – d. 29 December 1127), Abbess of Quedlinburg (1110) and Gandersheim (1111).
2 CONT #'''Adelaide (b. c. 1091 – d. 25/26 March 1127), married bef. 1118 to Dietrich III, Count of Vohburg and Margrave of the Northern March.[8]'''
2 CONT #[https://www.geni.com/people/Maria-of-Poland/6000000003087188060 A daughter] (b. c. 1092 – d. bef. 1111), married c. 1111 with a Polish lord.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/POLAND.htm#DauWladislawIdiedbefore12Oct1112
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Vladislaus-I-Herman/6000000003087080306 Prince Władysław] & his [https://www.geni.com/people/Judith-of-Swabia/305976324250005669 second wife] had [four] children: 
2 CONT *2. [https://www.geni.com/people/Judith-Maria-of-Kiev/6000000010107772824 daughter] (after 1088-before 12 Oct 1112) ...... .  . . 
2 CONT *3. [https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-I-Abbess-of-Quedlinburg/367922923820005107 AGNES] ([1090]-[1126/27]). ... ... Abbess of Gandersheim 1111/12, then Abbess of Quedlinburg.  
2 CONT *4. ['''ADELAJDA''' ([1090/91]-25/26 Mar [1127]).  The Notæ Genealogicæ Bavaricæ refers to the first wife of "Marchio Dietpoldus" as "de Polonia"[193].  The primary source which confirms her parentage more specifically has not yet
2 CONC  been identified.  ''She is not one of Władysław's daughters referred to in the Chronicæ Polanorum[194]*''.  The Fundatio Monasterii Richenbacensis names "Adelheidis" as wife of "marchio Dietpaldus" in connection with the foundati
2 CONC on of Reichenbach[195].  The necrology of Admont records the death "VIII Kal Mar" of "Adelheit marchyonissa"[196].  '''m''' ([before 1105]) as his first wife, DIETPOLD [III] Graf von Vohburg, Cham und Nabberg Markgraf der Nordgau,
2 CONC  son of DIEPOLD [II] von Giengen Markgraf im Nordgau & his wife Liutgarde von Zähringen (-1146).] 
2 CONT *5. [https://www.geni.com/people/Maria-of-Poland/6000000003087188060 daughter] (1090-). ...  ... '''m''' (1111) ---, a Polish lord. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''*be careful not to translate the attention warnings confusing documents, into notices of identity denial ''
2 CONT -----------
