2 CONC onem, Conradum, Riddagum, et filiam Hiddam" as children of "comes Tidericus", specifying that "primus filius Fridericus fuit prepositus maioris Magdeburgensis ecclesie, postea Monasteriensis episcopus"[267].  Provost at Magdeburg 
2 CONC cathedral before 1063.  Elected Bishop of Magdeburg 1063.  Provost of Münster cathedral 1063.  Imperial chancellor.  Bishop of Münster 1064.  
