1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gertrude_of_Poland
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 4 Jan 1107-1108 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Svyatopolk II Mikhail, Grand Duke Of KIEV b: 1050 in Of, Kiev, Kiev, Ukraine
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Yaropolk Petr Izyaslavich, Duke Of VLADIMIR VOLYNSK AND TUROV b: Bef 1050 in Of, Vladimir Volynskij, Volyn, Ukraine
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Svyatoslav Izyaslavich, Prince Of KIEV b: Abt 1052 in Of, Kiev, Kiev, Ukraine
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Vsevolod Izyaslavich, Prince Of KIEV b: Abt 1054 in Of, Kiev, Kiev, Ukraine
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Igor Izyaslavich, Prince Of KIEV b: Abt 1056 in Of, Kiev, Kiev, Ukraine
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Evpraksya Izyaslavna Princess Of KIEV b: Abt 1072 in Of, Turov, Polbesye, Byelorussia
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Mstislav Izyaslavich, Duke Of POLOTSK b: Abt 1044 in Of, Polotsk, Polotsk, Byelorussia
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude (about 1025- 4 January 1108), princess of Poland, was the daughter of King Mieszko II of Poland and Richensa of Lotharingia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1043, she was married to Iziaslav of Kiev in a double ceremony that also married her brother to Iziaslav's sister. She had one son, Yaropolk Iziaslavich, by her husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrude was the owner of a medieval illuminated manuscript, known as the Egbert Psalter or Trier Psalter, that had been created in the late 10th century for archbishop Egbert of Trier. She included her prayer book as part of the 
2 CONC codex. In the prayer book she prays six times for Yaropolk, "unicus filius meus" (my only son).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Kiovan ruhtinaan puoliso.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gertrud var datter til kong Mieszko II Lambert av Polen og søster til Kasimir Karol av Polen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilder:
2 CONT
2 CONT N. de Baumgarten: Généalogie et Mariage occidenteaux des Rurikides Russes du Xe au XIII Siècle. Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, nr. 187. Bent og Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 18, 79. 
