1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mstislav Iziaslavich''' (Russian: '''Мстислав Изяславич''') Prince of Polotsk, Grand Prince of Novgorod, died about 1069.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Mstislav Iziaslavich and his wife had one child: 
2 CONT #Rostislav Mstislavich
2 CONT
2 CONT Mstislav Iziaslavich was the son of Iziaslav I and Gertruda of Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Primary Chronicle names Mstislav son of Izyaslav, recording that his father established him as Prince of Polotsk in 1069 but that "he soon died".  He was installed as Prince of Novgorod by his father.  He was expelled from Nov
2 CONC gorod by Vseslav Prince of Polotsk in 1066 or 1067.  He was not restored in Novgorod when his father returned from exile in Poland, but was replaced by Gleb Sviatoslavich.  
2 CONT
