2 CONC 5/6)  Alfonso (c.1144-by 1149)  In 1152, Alfonso married Richeza of Poland, the daughter of Ladislaus II the Exile.[7] They had:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand, (1153-1157)  Sancha (1155-1208), the wife of Alfonso II of Aragón.  Alfonso also had two mistresses, having children by both. By an Asturian noblewoman named Guntroda Pérez, he had an illegitimate daughter, Urraca (1132
2 CONC -1164), who married García Ramírez of Navarre, the mother retiring to a convent in 1133.[8] Later in his reign, he formed a liaison with Urraca Fernández, widow of count Rodrigo Martínez and daughter of Fernando Garcés de Hita, an
2 CONC  apparent grandson of García Sánchez III of Navarre, having a daughter Stephanie the Unfortunate (1148-1180), who was killed by her jealous husband, Fernán Ruiz de Castro.
2 CONT
