2 CONT Adelaide (c. 1040 – 27 January 1062), wife of king Vratislaus II of Bohemia King Solomon of Hungary (1053 – 1087 or after) David (after 1053 – after 1094) Legacy Andrew's son Solomon never properly managed to establish himself as 
2 CONC king; the sons of Andrew's younger brother gradually took over, particularly since neither Solomon, nor David (Andrew's youngest son) left surviving male descendants. Thus, Andrew's line continued in the Piast dynasty but not in H
2 CONC ungary.
