2 CONT
2 CONT ==Richeza of Poland, Queen of Hungary==
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT Adelaide/Richeza of Poland, (c. 1018 – after 1059) was Queen Consort of Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a daughter of King Mieszko II Lambert of Poland, and his wife, Richeza of Lotharingia. She is traditionally called Richeza, but contemporary sources do not confirm this name. Nowadays it is supposed that she was called Ade
2 CONC laide[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 1039 and 1043, she was married to Duke Béla of Hungary, who had served her father and taken part in her father's campaigns against the pagan Pomeran tribes.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1048, her husband received one third of Hungary ("Tercia pars Regni") as appanage from his brother, King Andrew I of Hungary, and the couple moved to Hungary. On 6 December 1060, her husband was crowned King of Hungary after de
2 CONC feating his brother. She possibly was not alive at the time of her husband's coronation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT *1039-1043: King Béla I of Hungary (c. 1016 – 11 September 1063)
2 CONT **1. King Géza I of Hungary (c. 1040 – 25 April 1077)
2 CONT **2. King Ladislaus I of Hungary (c. 1040 – 29 July 1095)
2 CONT **3. Duke Lampert of Hungary (after 1050 – c. 1095)
2 CONT **4. Sophia (after 1050 – 18 June 1095), wife firstly of Markgraf Ulrich I of Carniola, and secondly of duke Magnus I of Saxony
2 CONT **5. Euphemia (after 1050 – 2 April 1111), wife of Prince Otto I of Moravia
2 CONT **6. Ilona (after 1050 – c. 1091), wife of king Dmitar Zvonimir of Croatia
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richeza_of_Poland,_Queen_of_Hungary
