2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_the_Great '''Vladimir the Great'''] was Prince of Novgorod, Grand Prince of Kiev, and ruler of Kievan Rus' from 980 to 1015.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saint Vladimir Svyatoslavich the Great, also sometimes spelled Volodymer (Old East Slavic: Володимеръ Святославичь). His name is spelt variously: in modern Ukrainian as Volodymyr (Володимир); in Old Church Slavonic and modern Russ
2 CONC ian, as Vladimir (Владимир); in Old Norse as Valdamarr; and, in modern Scandinavian languages, "Valdemar".
2 CONT
2 CONT *Born: c. 956
2 CONT *Died:15 July 1015, Berestovo
2 CONT
