2 CONT Henry VI, (d. 1288) Count of Luxembourg  Waleran I (d. 1288), Count of Ligny & Roussy  Isabelle (1247-1298), married Guy de Dampierre  Philippa of Luxembourg (1252-1311), married John II, Count of Holland  Margaret  Felicitas  Joa
2 CONC nna (d. 1310), Abbess of Clairefontaine  He also had at least three bastard sons, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry, bastard of Luxembourg (d. 1288), married Isabelle of Houffalize, heiress of Houffalize
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Henry V the Blond (1216 – 24 December 1281), called the Great, was the count of Luxembourg, Laroche and Arlon from 1247 to his death and the count of Namur between 1256 and 1264 as Henry III. He was the son and successor of Walera
2 CONC n III of Limburg and Ermesinda of Luxembourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1240 Margaret, daughter of Henry II, Count of Bar, who brought him Ligny-en-Barrois as her dowry, though, by a clause in the marriage contract, it remained under the feudal suzerainty of the county of Bar. In contemp
2 CONC t of this, Henry paid homage in 1256 to Theobald II of Navarre, in his capacity as Count of Champagne. Henry's brother-in-law, Theobald II of Bar, took advantage of the conflict then raging between Frederick III of Lorraine and th
2 CONC e bishops of Metz. Henry V was a partisan of the duke and so Theobald took the side of the bishop. Henry was captured in battle at Prény on 14 September 1266. On 8 September 1268, King Louis IX arbitrated between the two counts an
2 CONC d Henry was freed and repossessed of Ligny, but under the suzerainty of the Barrois.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1256, Henry seized Namur while the reigning margrave, Baldwin II, was also reigning emperor in Constantinople. Baldwin relinquished his rights to Namur to Guy of Dampierre, Count of Flanders, who retook the margraviate from Hen
2 CONC ry. The two parties made peace and Guy married Henry's daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Margaret he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry VI, (d. 1288) Count of Luxembourg  Waleran I (d. 1288), Count of Ligny & Roussy  Isabelle (1247-1298), married Guy de Dampierre  Philippa of Luxembourg (1252-1311), married John II, Count of Holland  Margaret  Felicitas  Joa
2 CONC nna (d. 1310), Abbess of Clairefontaine  He also had at least three bastard sons, including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry, bastard of Luxembourg (d. 1288), married Isabelle of Houffalize, heiress of Houffalize  Preceded by Ermesinda Count of Luxembourg 1247–1281 Succeeded by Henry VI  Count of Laroche 1247–1281 Succeeded by Waleran I  Preceded 
2 CONC by Waleran III Count of Arlon 1256–1264 Succeeded by Henry VI  Preceded by Baldwin II Count of Namur 1256–1264 Succeeded by Guy 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Henry V, Count of Luxembourg
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry V the Blond (1216 – 24 December 1281), called the Great, was the count of Luxembourg, Laroche and Arlon from 1247 to his death and the count of Namur between 1256 and 1264 as Henry III. He was the son and successor of Walera
2 CONC n III of Limburg and Ermesinda of Luxembourg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1240 Margaret, daughter of Henry II, Count of Bar, who brought him Ligny-en-Barrois as her dowry, though, by a clause in the marriage contract, it remained under the feudal suzerainty of the county of Bar. In contemp
2 CONC t of this, Henry paid homage in 1256 to Theobald II of Navarre, in his capacity as Count of Champagne. Henry's brother-in-law, Theobald II of Bar, took advantage of the conflict then raging between Frederick III of Lorraine and th
2 CONC e bishops of Metz. Henry V was a partisan of the duke and so Theobald took the side of the bishop. Henry was captured in battle at Prény on 14 September 1266. On 8 September 1268, King Louis IX arbitrated between the two counts an
2 CONC d Henry was freed and repossessed of Ligny, but under the suzerainty of the Barrois.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1256, Henry seized Namur while the reigning margrave, Baldwin II, was also reigning emperor in Constantinople. Baldwin relinquished his rights to Namur to Guy of Dampierre, Count of Flanders, who retook the margraviate from Hen
2 CONC ry. The two parties made peace and Guy married Henry's daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Margaret he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry VI, (d. 1288) Count of Luxembourg 
2 CONT
2 CONT Waleran I (d. 1288), Count of Ligny & Roussy 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabelle (1247-1298), married Guy de Dampierre 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa of Luxembourg (1252-1311), married John II, Count of Holland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret 
2 CONT
2 CONT Felicitas 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna (d. 1310), Abbess of Clairefontaine 
2 CONT
