1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LOTHARINGIAN%20(LOWER)%20NOBILITY.htm#HeinrichSalmdied1228B
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich von Salm (c1190-after 21 Sep 1228).  
2 CONT *Richer records that "comite Henrico…dictus…de Salmis…contemporaneus noster" married "sororem Friderici ducis Lotoringie" and had two sons "primogenitum…Henricum et alium…Fridericum"[277].  
2 CONT *Seigneur de Viviers.  
2 CONT *Richer records that "comite Henrico…dictus…de Salmis…contemporaneus noster" granted "castrum de Vivario" to his son "Henricus" when he married[278].  
2 CONT *Richer records that "Hanrico filio Hanrici de Danubrio dicti de Salmis" obtained the advocacies of "vallis Senoniensis et de Plannia et Vypodi-cella", referring also to "patruus eius Fridericus"[279].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Married''' ([Jan/Jul] 1221) to '''Marguerite de Bar''', daughter of THIBAUT I Comte de Bar & his second wife Ermesinde de Bar-sur-Seine (-after 1259).  
2 CONT *She is named, but her origin not stated, in the charter dated Jan 1221 under which "H comes de Salmis et Joeta uxor mea" consented to the château de Viviers constituting the dower of "Margaretam" on her marriage to "Henrico primo
2 CONC genito nostro"[280].  
2 CONT *Richer records that "comite Henrico…dictus…de Salmis…contemporaneus noster" married "sororem Friderici ducis Lotoringie" and had two sons "primogenitum…Henricum et alium…Fridericum", and that "dictus Henricus" married "uxorem de 
2 CONC stirpe comitis Barrensis"[281].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich & his wife had [three] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Heinrich [IV] (c1222-8 Jan 1292 or 8 Jun 1293).  
2 CONT # Sophie (c1222-  ?)
2 CONT # Hermann (c1222-aft 1248)  
2 CONT # N.N. - Heinrich has one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress.
