1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LOTHARINGIAN%20(LOWER)%20NOBILITY.htm#HeinrichIIISalmdied1246
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Heinrich [III] & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT # HEINRICH von Salm (-after 21 Sep 1228). 
2 CONT # JUTTA von Salm (-after Dec 1224).  
2 CONT # AGNES von Salm (-15 Jan 1280, bur Abbey of Remiremont).  She was elected Abbess of Remiremont in 1242 in succession to her maternal aunt Agathe de Lorraine[286].  
2 CONT # LAURETTE von Salm (-after Dec 1224). 
2 CONT # FRIEDRICH von Salm (-1255).  
2 CONT # THOMASSE von Salm (-after 1256).  Treasurer of the abbey of Remiremont[295]. 
2 CONT # BERTHA von Salm .  
2 CONT
2 CONT *Richer records that "comite Henrico…dictus…de Salmis…contemporaneus noster" married "sororem Friderici ducis Lotoringie" and had two sons "primogenitum…Henricum et alium…Fridericum"[288].  
2 CONT *"H dictus comes de Salmes, J comitissa uxor mea, Henricus et Fredericus filii nostri" donated property to the abbey of Senone by charter dated 19 Feb 1219[289].  
2 CONT *Richer records that "Friderico [de Albo-monte] filio Henrici comitis" was expelled from "castro de Albo-monte" and retreated to "castrum…Piere-percie"[290].  
2 CONT *Seigneur de Blâmont [Blankenberg].  
2 CONT *Richer records that "comitem Henricum…filius eius Fridericus miles" continued to attack the monastery, and retained "Album-montem et superius castrum de Danubrio", specifying that "mater dicti Hanrici" had obtained the latter[291
2 CONC ].  
2 CONT *"Henricus comes de Salmis et…Ferricus filius eiusdem" confirmed their obligations to the bishop of Metz by charter dated Mar 1234[292].  
2 CONT *"Ferris de Salmes" confirmed that, if he acquired "le chastel de Blanmont" by settlement with "mon coisin Henri de Salme", he would hold it as a fief from "mon…cosin Jaique evesques de Metz", by charter dated 13 Jan 1246 (O.S.)[2
2 CONC 93].
2 CONT
2 CONT *SEIGNEURS de BLÂMONT[294]. 
