1 OCCU dame de Nogent. Daughter of Mathieu II de Monmorency and Gertrude (de Nesle) de Soissons
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} I have her as Gertrude de Montmorency, dame de Nogent. Daughter of Mathieu II de Monmorency and Gertrude (de Nesle) de Soissons. Married Simon III de Parroye and Thierry "le Diable" de Lorraine, sieur d'Autigny. Mo
2 CONC ther of Albert de Parroye de Taintrux and de Croismare, and Ferry de Lorraine d'Autigny. Very close to matching what is on Geni.
2 CONT
2 CONT I got most of my information from Daniel de Rauglaure at INRIA, who is usually an exceptionally reliable source for French lines.
2 CONT
2 CONT A quick check shows Rauglaudre has changed his info.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has the Gertrude who married Thierry le Diable ("Diederik") as daughter of Bouchard V de Montmorency and Laurence de Hainault, and mother only of Judith.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://roglo.eu/roglo?lang=en;i=4040367
2 CONT
2 CONT Then he has this Gertrude still as born about 1200, still as daughter of Mathieu II de Montmorency and Gertrude de Nesle, but no husband or children.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://roglo.eu/roglo?lang=en;i=1137155
2 CONT
2 CONT Double checking, I see he now has Albert de Parroye de Taintrux (who married Jeanne de Riste) as Aubert, son of Simon de Parroye and Alix de Nogent.
2 CONT
2 CONT So, clearly he has re-mastered this entire area.
2 CONT
2 CONT I often checked Rauglaudre's info against Prof. Herbert Stoyan's database, but it seems to be currently in one of its frequent "down" periods. Further, he now forwards on of his main links to Leo van de Pas' database. The other li
2 CONC nk isn't working but looks like it is supposed to forward to Daniel de Rauglaudre, so it all seems a bit circular.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ww-person.com/ (Main page)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://ww-person.com/cgi-bin/wwp/LANG=engl/?list (Search page)
2 CONT
2 CONT At this point, I don't think I would trust any of the sources completely. The problem with MedLands is often that it is incomplete, while I'm not seeing anything on the others that would explain the arguments in this area.
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments from Justin Swanstrom 29/09/2016
