2 CONT 8. SOBĚSLAV UDALRICH ([1075]-14 Feb 1140). ... He succeeded in 1125 as SOBĚSLAV I UDALRICH Duke of the Bohemians. ... m ([1123]) ADELAIDA of Hungary, daughter of ÁLMOS Prince of Hungary & his wife Predslava Sviatopolkovna of Kiev 
2 CONC ([1105/07]-15 Sep 1140). ... Duke Sobĕslav I Udalrich & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT *a)       VLADISLAV (-1165). ...  m ([1152/55]) --- von Brandenburg, daughter of ALBRECHT I "dem Bären" Graf von Ballenstedt Markgraf von Brandenburg & his wife Sophie von Winzenburg.  
2 CONT *b)         SOBĚSLAV (1128-9 Jan 1180).  ... He succeeded in 1173 as SOBĚSLAV II Duke of Bohemia. ... m ([1173/77]) as her first husband, ELŹBIETA of Poland, daughter of MIESZKO III "Stary/the Old" Prince of Greater Poland & his f
2 CONC irst wife Erszebet of Hungary ([1152]-2 Apr 1209, bur Kloster Dobrilugk). ...
2 CONT *c)         '''MARIA''' .  The Canonici Wissegradensis Continuatio Cosmæ records the marriage in 1138 of "dux Sobezlaus filiam suam Mariam" with "filio Leupoldi orientalis marchionis" specifying that it was celebrated in "Moravia 
2 CONC in Olomucensi parte"[198].  The primary source which names her husband has not yet been identified.  However, it appears that Leopold is the only son to whom the text can refer.  The primary source which confirms her second marria
2 CONC ge has not yet been identified. <br>''' m''' firstly (29 Sep 1138) LEOPOLD IV Markgraf of Austria, son of LEOPOLD III "der Heilige" Markgraf of Austria & his second wife Agnes of Germany [Staufen] (-Niedraltaich 18 Oct 1141).  Duk
2 CONC e of Bavaria 1139. <br> '''m''' secondly (after 1141) as his second wife, HERMANN III Markgraf von Baden and Verona, son of HERMANN II Markgraf von Baden & his wife Judith [von Dillingen] (-after 12 Jul 1153, bur Backnang Stiftski
2 CONC rche).  
2 CONT *d)         ULRICH (1134-18 Oct 1177).  ... He succeeded in 1165 as ULRICH Duke of the Bohemians.  Duke of Moravia 1176.  m firstly CECILIA von Thüringen, daughter of LUDWIG I Landgraf of Thuringia & his wife Hedwig von Gudensberg
2 CONC . ... m secondly as her first husband, SOPHIA von Meissen, daughter of OTTO "der Reicher" Markgraf von Meissen [Wettin] & his wife Hedwig von Brandenburg [Ballenstedt].  ... Duke Ulrich & his second wife had one child: 
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT *e)         WENZEL (1137-in prison [1192]).  ... He succeeded in 1191 as WENZEL II Duke of Bohemia. ... 
