1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnes_of_Rochlitz
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes of Rochlitz (d.1195) came from the Wettin family and was daughter of Dedi V, Count of Wettin and his wife, Matilda of Heinsburg. She is also known as Agnes of Wettin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes married Berthold IV, Duke of Merania. From this marriage Agnes gained the titles of Duchess of Merania and Count of Andechs.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1186, Agnes' husband accompanied Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor to the Kingdom of Sicily. In 1189, he led the third division of the imperial army and was its standard-bearer on the Third Crusade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes had eight children. Among them, three queens:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Otto I, who succeeded his father
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ekbert, bishop of Bamberg
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Henry, margrave of Istria
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Hedwig, married Henry I the Bearded, duke of Silesia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Gertrude, married Andrew II of Hungary
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Agnes, married Philip II of France
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Berthold, patriarch of Aquileia
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mathilde, abbess of Klitzingen
2 CONT
2 CONT An unnamed daughter married into the Nemanjic family of Serbia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her daughter, Agnes was the disputed third wife of Philip II of France. Another daughter, Gertrude became Queen of Hungary, by her marriage to Andrew II of Hungary, she was however murdered because she gave Hungarian lands to her 
2 CONC relatives. Agnes' eldest daughter, Hedwig became Queen of Poland and was eventually canonized in 1267.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes is a descendent of Agnes of Germany and Frederick I, Duke of Swabia, through their daughter, Bertha of Swabia. Agnes of Germany was a daughter of Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor and his first wife, Bertha of Savoy. Henry's pare
2 CONC nts were Henry III, Holy Roman Emperor and Agnes of Poitou.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes of Poitou was a daughter of William V, Duke of Aquitaine and his third wife Agnes of Burgundy.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnes_of_Rochlitz
