2 CONT 1.         VITALE Michieli [II] (-1172, bur San Zaccheria).  Andrea Dandulo´s Chronicon Venetum records the succession of "Vitalis Michaël secundus dux" in 1156[176].  Andrea Navagiero´s Storia della Repubblica Veneziana records t
2 CONC hat "Vitale Michiel" was elected Doge in 1154[177].  He was elected Doge of Venice in 1155.  "Vitalis Michael…Venetie, Dalmacie atque Chroacie Dux" donated the church of St Mark at Tyre to the church of San Marco, Venice by charte
2 CONC r dated Aug 1164, signed by "Sebastianus Ziani judex, Auriomastro Petro judex, Marinus Michael judex, Vitalis Dandulo judex…"[178].  Andrea Navagiero´s Storia della Repubblica Veneziana records that "Vitale Michiel" died after rul
2 CONC ing as Doge for 17 years, 17 days, and was buried "a San Zaccheria"[179].  Andrea Dandulo´s Chronicon Venetum records the death 27 Mar, in the 17th year of his rule, of "ducem" and his burial in "monasterium Sancti Zachariæ"[180].
2 CONC
