2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casimir_I_of_Kuyavia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT * Casimir's first marriage was to Jadwiga, whose origins are unknown. They had no children and she died in 1235.[3]
2 CONT * Casimir married secondly in 1239 to Constance, daughter of Henry II the Pious and Anna of Bohemia. They had the following children:
2 CONT # Adelaide (before 7 April 1249-8 December 1291), nun
2 CONT # Leszek II the Black (1240/42-30 September 1288), Duke of the Fragmentation of Poland
2 CONT # Ziemomysł of Kuyavia (1241/45-29 October/24 December 1287), Duke of Kuyavia
2 CONT * After Constance died in 1257, Casimir married in the same year, Euphrosyne, daughter of Casimir I of Opole and Viola, and they had the following children:
2 CONT # Władysław I the Elbow-high (1261-March 2, 1333), King of Poland (1320–1333)
2 CONT # Casimir (1261/62-10 June 1294), killed while in battle in Lithuania
2 CONT # Siemowit (1262/67-1309/14), Duke of Kuyavia-Brieg, married Anastasia of Galicia (daughter of Lev I of Galicia)
2 CONT # Euphemia (d.18 March 1308), married Yuri I of Galicia
