1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mścisław II Wsiewołodowicz''' was the Prince of Black Ruthenia. Reign 1172 – 1175. Preceded by Hleb Wsiewołodowicz. Succeeded by Erdywił. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mścisław Wsiewołodowicz''' (Wsiewołodkowicz) (died after 1183) - the prince of Black Ruthenia from 1172, son of Vsevolod, prince of Black Ruthenia and Agafia Vladimirovna, daughter of Vladimir Monomach.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography.  Mścisław was the youngest of the three sons of Vsevolod, Prince of Black Ruthenia, from his marriage to Agafia Władimirowna, daughter of Vladimir Monomakh. It is quite likely that it was Mścisław and his older brother 
2 CONC Gleb who had in mind in 1167, when, after the death of the Kiev prince Rastisław Mścisławicz, the Volyn prince Mścisław Izyasławycz, who took the Kiev table, they turned to the Wsiewołodkowiczes for help. In 1168, Mścisław took pa
2 CONC rt in the expedition of Mścisław, then the prince of Kiev, in the expedition against the Polovtsians [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT At the beginning of 1170, Mstisław Izyasławycz appealed to the Vsevolodkovic family for help in regaining Kiev from Gleb Jurewicz, who was imprisoned there by his brother, Prince Vladimir Andrei Juriewicz Bogolyubsky, who conquere
2 CONC d Kiev. But after Mstislav Izyasławycz conquered Kiev in February-March 1170, he quarreled only with one Vsevolodovich - Mstislav. It is likely that at that time Gleb had already died, after which Mstislav inherited the legacy of 
2 CONC the Black Ruthenians. According to AV, Nazarenko Mstislav was forbidden to come to the aid of Mstislav Izyaslavych due to his brother's illness, which ended in his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1183 Mścisław took part in the all-Russian campaign against the Polovtsians.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not known whether Mścisław was married or had children. In 1173 the Rostislavichs of Smostin refused to recognize Andrei Bogoliubski's experiences and captured Kiev. In response, Bogolyubsky appealed to various princes, incl
2 CONC uding the princes of Black Russia. It is possible that at that time, apart from Mstislav, there was at least one adult clan member in the Duchy of Black Russia, but it is not clear whose son he was.
2 CONT
2 CONT In "Composition of the Igora company".  And you, brave Roman and Mścisław! Bold design leads the mind to the feat. You fly high on a feat of courage, like a hawk soaring in the wind, trying to defeat a bird brazenly. After all, yo
2 CONC ur warriors have iron bows under their Latin helmets. Therefore, the earth trembled, and many nations - Hinova, Lithuania, Yatvyagi, Deremela and Polovtsy - threw spears and bowed their heads under these damask swords. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Comments. 
2 CONT  Nazarenko AV The Duchy of Grodno and the Dukes of Grodno in the 12th century. - pp. 169-170.
2 CONT  "A word about Igor's regiment" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Literature.  Nazarenko AV The Duchy of Grodno and the Dukes of Grodno in the 12th century. // The oldest countries in Eastern Europe. - M.: Eastern Literature, 2000. - Pages 169-188. 
