1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Vladimir Konstantinovich''' (1214-1249) - the first prince of Uglitch / Uglich (1218-1249).
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of the Grand Duke of Vladimir Konstantin Vsevolodovich, was born in 1214. Together with his uncle Yaroslav Vsevolodovich, he went to the Chernigov prince Mikhail Vsevolodovich (1230). Participated in the Battle of the City
2 CONC  (1238); after the defeat of the Russians, he fled.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1244, he went to the horde with the Grand Duke Yaroslav "about his fatherland", that is, to confirm the khan's rights to a hereditary inheritance.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1249 in Vladimir. The prince's body was taken to Uglich and laid in the Church of the Savior.
2 CONT
2 CONT From marriage (since 1232) with the daughter of Ingvar Igorevich Ryazansky Evdokia, he had two sons - Andrei and Roman, who successively reigned in Uglich.
