1 NOTE Wenceslaus II Premyslid (Czech: Václav II.; Polish: Waclaw II Czeski; September 27[1], 1271 - June 21, 1305) was King of Bohemia (1278 - 1305), Duke of Cracow (1291 - 1305) and crowned King of Poland (1300 - 1305) at Mainz.
