1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Trojden I''' – '''książę czerski''' od 1310, od 1313 dodatkowo '''w Warszawie i Liwie''', w latach 1336-1340 '''regent w Płocku'''. http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trojden_I
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trojden_I_of_Masovia
2 CONT
2 CONT Trojden I of Masovia
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to:navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Trojden I of Masovia (1284 or 86 -13 March 1341) was a member of the House of Piast. He was Duke of Czersk from 1310. From 1336 to 1340 he was Regent the Duchy of Płock. He eventually became Duke of Masovia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Trojden was the second son of Boleslaus II of Masovia and his first wife, Sophie, the daughter of Grand Duke Treniota of Lithuania.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Life
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1310, when his father was still alive Trojden received the small region Czersk. When his father died in 1313 he inherited parts of Warsaw and Liw in addition to his duchy, which allowed Trojden to reign over Eastern Masovia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Initially Trojden maintained excellent relations with Ladislaus the Short, king of Poland. Thanks to his intervention, in 1310 Trojden married Maria, daughter of Yuri I of Galicia and Euphemia of Kuyavia (Trojden's cousin). When R
2 CONC oman the Great died, there was two heirs. Ladislaus supported Boleslaus, the son of Trojden, who seized the throne and took the name of George II (Jerzy II).
2 CONT
2 CONT The aggressive policy pursued by Ladislaus the Short to reunite the territories of Poland and Masovia were a threat. On January 2 1326 at Brodnica, Trojden and his brothers, Siemowit II of Masovia and Wenceslaus of Płock concluded
2 CONC  an agreement with the Teutonic Knights, which lead to a short conflict with Poland and its ally Lithuania.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1340, his eldest son Boleslaw (aka George II) was murdered by his subjects. Trojden waives his right to succeed his son in exchange for a large sum of money paid to him by Casimir III the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT Trojden died on March 13 1341 and is buried in the church of Dominicans in Rawa.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Before 1310, Trojden married Maria daughter of Yuri I of Galicia, they had four children[1]:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Euphemia (1310-after 1373) married Casimir I, Duke of Cieszyn and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Boleslaw-Yuri II of Galicia (1308 - April 7, 1340), became King of Halych-Volhynia
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Siemowit III of Masovia (before 1314-16 June 1381), became Duke of Masovia
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Casimir (1314-26 November 1355), Prince of Ciechanów and Warsaw
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ POLAND, Medieval Lands
2 CONT
