1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Constantine Vladimirovich''' (d. after 1241) - son of Vladimir Glebovich, the principal prince of Pronsk.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1217, Constantine was an accomplice of his brother Gleb, who called almost all his relatives to a congress in Isady and treacherously killed them at his feast with the expectation of taking possession of all the Ryazan lands. F
2 CONC orced to flee to the Polovtsy (Cumans), in 1218 Constantine gathered the Polovtsian army and approached Ryazan, but was defeated by Ingvar Igorevich and again fled to the Polovtsy (Cumans).
2 CONT
2 CONT (Historian F.B. Uspensky clarifies that although Prince Constantine, who agreed to help the organizer of the massacre, Gleb Vladimirovich, is called his “brother”, it is not necessary that he was his own brother (and the son of Vl
2 CONC adimir Glebovich), and not a cousin. The patronymics of this Constantine in the sources are not indicated).
2 CONT
2 CONT Later Constantine wandered somewhere for a long time, and in 1240 he appeared in Volhynia and helped Rostislav, son of Mikhail of Chernigov, with whom he took Galich. Forced out of this city by Daniel and Vasilko Romanoviches, Con
2 CONC stantine was sent by Rostislav to Przemysel, to the local "seditious" bishop, but fled from there when Daniel's troops approached. Constantine's further fate is unknown. His only son, Eustathius, lived in Lithuania and participate
2 CONC d in the wars of Mindaugas.
