1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Izyaslav Vladimirovich''' (d. July 20, 1217, Isady) - prince of Pronsk (1207), son of Vladimir Glebovich.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1207, after Vsevolod "the Big Nest" captured Roman, Svyatoslav Gleboviches, Ingvar and Yuri Igoreviches, slandered by Gleb and Oleg Vladimiroviches, and the flight of Mikhail Vsevolodovich to Chernigov, Izyaslav led the defense
2 CONC  of Pronsk, which was not crowned with success. Oleg Vladimirovich was imprisoned for the reign in Pronsk. In the winter of 1208/1209, Mikhail Vsevolodovich and Izyaslav Vladimirovich invaded the Vladimir-Suzdal principality but w
2 CONC ere defeated in the vicinity of Moscow by Prince Yuri Vsevolodovich of Vladimir. On July 20, 1217, Izyaslav was killed by his brothers Gleb and Konstantin at the princely congress in Isady, duchy of Ryazan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information about the family and descendants of Izyaslav has not been preserved.
