2 CONT
2 CONT Roger I of Sicily
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger I (1031[1] – June 22, 1101), called Bosso and the Great Count, was the Norman Count of Sicily from 1071 to 1101. He was the last great leader of the Norman conquest of southern Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conquest of Calabria and Sicily
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger was the youngest son of Tancred of Hauteville by his second wife Fredisenda. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger died on June 22, 1101, in his seventieth year and was buried in S. Trinità of Mileto.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger's eldest son was a bastard named Jordan, who predeceased him. His second son, Geoffrey, may have been a bastard, but may also have been a son of his first or second wife. Whatever the case, he was a leper with no chance of i
2 CONC nheriting.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger's first marriage took place in 1061, to Judith, daughter of William, Count of Évreux and Hawisa of Échauffour. She died in 1076, leaving all daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT A daughter, married Hugh of Gircea (died 1075/6), the first count of Paternò
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda (1062 – before 1094) married firstly (repudiated before 1080) as his second wife, Robert, Count of Eu married secondly (1080, divorced 1088) as his second wife, Raymond IV of Toulouse
2 CONT
2 CONT Adelisa (died 1096), married in 1083 to Henry, Count of Monte Sant'Angelo
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma (died 1120), briefly engaged to Philip I of France; married firstly William VI of Auvergne and secondly Rudolf, Count of Montescaglioso.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1077, Roger married a second time, to Eremburga of Mortain, daughter of "William, Count of Mortain" (probably William Warlenc). Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mauger, Count of Troina
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda, married Guigues III, Count of Albon
2 CONT
2 CONT Muriel (died 1119), married Josbert de Lucy
2 CONT
2 CONT Constancia, married Conrad of Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT Felicia, married King Coloman of Hungary
2 CONT
2 CONT Violante, married Robert of Burgundy, son of Robert I of Burgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT Flandina, married Henry del Vasto
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith (died 1136), married Robert I of Bassunvilla
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger's third and last wife was Adelaide del Vasto, niece of Boniface, Lord of Savona. They married in 1087. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon, Count of Sicily
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda, married Ranulf II, Count of Alife
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger II, Count, later King, of Sicily
2 CONT
2 CONT Maximilla, married Hildebrand VI (of the Aldobrandeschi family)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_I_of_Sicily
2 CONT
2 CONT http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruggero_I_di_Sicilia
