2 CONT Géza I (Hungarian: I. Géza) (c. 1040 – 25 April 1077), King of Hungary (1074-1077). During King Solomon's rule he governed, as Duke, one third of the Kingdom of Hungary. Afterwards, Géza rebelled against his cousin's reign and his
2 CONC  followers proclaimed him king. However, he never achieved to strengthen his position, because King Solomon could maintain his rule over the Western part of the kingdom. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Géza was the eldest son of the future King Béla I of Hungary and his wife Adelaide/Rixa of Poland. When Géza was born, his parents were living in the court of his mother's brother, King Casimir I of Poland, because Béla had been o
2 CONC bliged to leave Hungary after his father made an unsuccessful attempt against his cousin, King Stephen, the first King of Hungary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages and children 
