1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Manfred Mayr, page 27, “Geschichte der Burggrafen von Regensburg”, Udilhilde (Adelheid) von Regensburg, Queen of Hungary, who died after 1131, was the only daughter of the Burggraf Heinrich II. von Reg
2 CONC ensburg (1083- 1101 in Jerusalem) of the House of the Babonen, a sister of Burggraf Otto I. von Regensburg (died 21.10.1143) and a granddaughter of Burggraf Heinrich I. von Regensburg (died 30 September in about 1083 and Wiltrud.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.manfred-hiebl.de/genealogie-mittelalter/babonen_reg/heinrich_2_burggraf_1101/heinrich_2_1101.html [145 Fundatio: "...unde factum est, ut rex Ungarie duxerit in uxorem filiam predicti Heinrici primi nomine Udelhildam ...
2 CONC  et ab duxerit in terram suam factam consortem et principem regni sui."
2 CONT
2 CONT Andreas Thiele, table 355 "Erzählende genealogische Stammtafeln zur europäischen Geschichte Band II, Teilband 2 Europäische Kaiser-, Königs- und Fürstenhäuser II Nord-, Ost- und Südeuropa"  states King Stefan II. of Hungary’s wife
2 CONC  was Adelheid von Riedenburg, daughter of Stefan von Riedenburg, Burggraf of Regensburg. As King Stephan II. of Hungary was born in 1101 and died in 1131 it is extremely unlikely that he married a wife who was born in 1066 who was
2 CONC  old enough to be his grandmother, so this supposed birthdate on her Geni  profile has been changed to ca. 1101 to match her husband’s age.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is an apparent confusion with the supposed name of her father, quoted as Stefan. The Burgraves of Regensburg were also the Burggraves of nearby Stefing and this name seems to be misquoted as a first name Stefan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is also extremely unlikely that Adelheid died in 1119 as she was King Stephan’s 2nd wife- book sources quote her as outliving him (he died in 1131), returning to Germany where she died after 1131 and was buried in Walderbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the absence of any evidence of there being a Stefan of Regensburg at all and based on Manfred Hiebl’s assertations, her father must have been Heinrich II. von Riedenburg, Burgrave of Regensburg. Source: http://www.manfred-hiebl
2 CONC .de/genealogie-mittelalter/babonen_reg/udilhilde_ungarn_1140/udilhilde_koenigin_1140.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/arpad/arpad2.html
2 CONT
