2 CONC ed to Hungary.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried in Székesfehérvár. Her remains were confidently identified by archeologists during late 19th century excavations at the ruined cathedral of Székesfehérvár. Her remains were afterwards reinterred at the Mathias Churc
2 CONC h in Budapest, with those of her husband.
