0 @N6000000000437189575@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Duchess Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of Poland
0 @N6000000002187639721@ NOTE Richeza of Poland
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Richeza of Poland (c. 1140 – June 16, 1185), was the daughter of King Wladislaus II the Exile of Poland, and Agnes of Babenberg. She accompanied her father into exile in 1146. Her name is also spelled Ryksa, Rixa, and Richilda.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married King Alfonso VII of Castile and León in 1152. Their only child, Infanta Sancha of Castile, was born 1155. In Spain she was known as "Queen Ricca".
1 CONT
1 CONT When Alphonso died in 1157, Richeza remarried to Ramon Berenguer II, Count of Provence, in 1162. Their daughter was Douce (died 1172). Ramond Berengar died in 1166, and she remarried once more to Count Raymond V of Toulouse.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her daughter, Sancha of Castile, married King Alfonso II of Aragon in 1174. Sancha's daughter, Eleanor married Count Raymond VI of Toulouse in 1202.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT Allstrom, Carl Magnus. Dictionary of Royal Lineage (Poland), 1902 
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Berenguela of Barcelona Queen Consort of Galicia
1 CONT 1152-1157 Succeeded by
1 CONT Urraca of Portugal 
1 CONT Queen Consort of León
1 CONT 1152-1157 
1 CONT Queen Consort of Castile
1 CONT 1152-1157 Succeeded by
1 CONT Leonor of England 
