0 @N6000000002187639837@ NOTE Boleslaus II of Poland
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT (Redirected from Boleslaus II)
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT
1 CONT Boleslaus II on Jan Matejko's paintingBoleslaus II was a duke and king of Poland 1058-1079 (crowned 1076). In Polish he is known as Boleslaw Smialy (the Bold), Szczodry (the Generous), or Okrutny (the Cruel).
1 CONT
1 CONT He supported pope Gregory VII in his struggle with the Emperor, but had the Bishop of Kraków St. Stanislaus put to death as a traitor. The king was forced into exile and Ladislaus Herman of Poland, 1079-1102, became duke of Poland
1 CONC . After him, two brothers, Zbigniew and Boleslaus, ruled jointly from 1102-1107.
1 CONT
