0 @N6000000002187588772@ NOTE Hermann III, Margrave of Baden
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann III of Baden (d. January 16, 1160), nicknamed the Great, was Margrave of Verona and Baden.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the son of Hermann II of Baden and Judit von Hohenberg. He served as regent for the maargravate of Baden from 1130 until 1160.
1 CONT
1 CONT Faithfully devoted to the Staufens, Hermann III came in conflict with his relatives from Zähringen-Swabia. In 1140 he participated in the siege of Weibtreu castle, and received the bailiwick of Selz in Alsace.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1151 the margravate of Verona was taken from Ottokar III von Steiermark and conferred on Hermann III. A deed of donation exists from 1153, that states Friedrich I bought Castle Besigheim from Hermann III.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann III fought in Lombardy in 1154 and aided Friedrich I in the latter's siege of Mailand.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann III took part in the Second Crusade, and fought in the first Italian campaign of the Emperor.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Marriage and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Bertha von Lothringen (d. after 1162) in 1134. Secondly, he married Maria of Bohemia after 1141. She was the daughter of Duke Sobeslav I of Bohemia.
1 CONT
1 CONT He had the following children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Hermann (d. September 13, 1190)
1 CONT     * Gertrud (d. before 1225) who married in 1180 Graf Albrecht von Dagsburg (d. 1211)
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann III was buried in the Augustine Monastery in Backnang.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Hermann II of Baden Margrave of Baden
1 CONT 1130–1160 Succeeded by
1 CONT Hermann IV of Baden
1 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT Margrave of Verona. Son of Hermann II, Margrave of Verona, Herr of Baden and Judith (of Hohenberg). Source: Leo van de Pas. *Stammtafeln zur Geschichte der Europaeischen Staaten*, 4 vol, Marburg, 1953,1975, by W.K. Prinz von Isenb
1 CONC urg. *Genealogisches Handbuch des Adels*, Fuerstliche Haeuser. 
0 @N6000000002486699942@ NOTE Hun var enke efter Friedrich af Schwaben (Kejser Conrads søn), da hun blev trolovet med den dengang kun 8 årige Knud i 1171.  I 1173 traf de igen hinanden, og året efter kom hun til DK som fredspant. Tre års senere blev de gift. 
1 CONT Gommen var kun 14 år gl. Ingen børn.
