1 CONT son of Henry IV, he continued his father's Investiture Controversy with the
1 CONT papacy, dying childless. As a ruler, Henry showed political skill, but his
1 CONT reach exceeded his grasp. He had dethroned his father by allying with the
1 CONT princes and presenting himself as a champion of the church's rights. Once in
1 CONT power, he was unable to force the church to grant him his demands. See #1718.
