0 @N6000000005598936617@ NOTE In about 1123, Henry was convinced by his father-in-law to move with h is forces as far south as Metz.  At a small town south of Rouen, Bourg therould, Henry's forces met those of Waleran.  Waleran in the engagem ent fell and was 
1 CONC captured by Henry's chamberlain William de Tancarvill e.  In 1124, Henry attempted an invasion of Champagne, but finding tha t he had stired up a hornets nests and the French lords and people ral lied to Louis VI, he and his army 
1 CONC never encountered that assembled by Louis VI of France.  As a result, Henry quickly withdrew back to Germa ny.
