1 CONT "Plantagenet Ancestry", Turton.
0 @N6000000002187580999@ NOTE Hermann I, Margrave of Baden
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann I of Baden (born 1040 in Freiburg im Breisgau; died April 25, 1074 in Cluny) was the Margrave of Verona and the founder of the line of Margraves of Baden.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann was the oldest son of Berthold I. He married Judit of Backnang-Sulichgau, Countess of Eberstein-Calw, who was the founder of Hirsau Abbey. From her, Hermann obtained the right to Baden-Baden, which would later become the c
1 CONC ore of the family dominions. Among those lands were the Frankish Albgau and Ufgau.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann I and his wife founded the Augustinian monastery of Backnang Abbey. It quickly became dilapidated, and was rebuilt by their son in 1123. Subsequently, the monastery was the resting place for five generations of the margrav
1 CONC es of Baden.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1073 Hermann separated from his wife, took monastic vows, and became a lay brother in Cluny Abbey. He is celebrated in the Catholic church on April 25.
1 CONT
1 CONT Hermann I and Judit had the following children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Hermann II (d. October 8, 1130)
1 CONT     * Luitgard
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] External links
1 CONT
