0 @N6000000000945059917@ NOTE Almos var prins av Ungarn og statholder 1087 i Dalmatien og Illyrien. 
1 CONT Fra 1091 til 1095 var han konge av Kroatia.
1 CONT Han ble forfulgt, fengslet i 1109 av Koloman og blindet. Koloman blindet også hans
1 CONT sønn i 1113 (eller 1123?).
1 CONT Almos ble første gang gift ca. 1090 med Sofie av Looz.
1 CONT Han døde i Tracien (eller i Konstantinopel).
0 @N6000000002322312934@ NOTE He and his infant son, Bela II, were blinded by the brother of Almos, Coloman
1 CONT in order for Coloman to secure the throne for his son, Stephen II.
0 @N6000000002187825367@ NOTE Prince Álmos
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Álmos (in Croatian and Slovak Almoš) (died 1129) was a Hungarian prince, the son of King Geza I of Hungary, brother of King Kálmán. He held several governmental posts in the Kingdom of Hungary.
1 CONT
1 CONT Between 1084 and 1091 he was the duke of Slavonia; between 1091 and 1095 he was named King of Slavonia (eastern Croatia). In 1095 Kálmán dethroned Álmos, making him the duke of the apanage Nitrian duchy (Tercia pars regni) instead
1 CONC .
1 CONT
1 CONT Álmos, supported by Germany and Bohemia, came in conflict with Kálmán in 1098, after Kálmán had declared himself the king of the whole of Croatia in 1097 (crowned in 1102). On August 21, 1104 Álmos married Predslava, the daughter 
1 CONC of Svyatopolk II of Kiev.
1 CONT
1 CONT Kálmán made peace with Álmos in 1108, but only to have Álmos and his son Béla imprisoned in 1108 or 1109 and then blinded to prevent them from becoming the future king. After this he went on to live in seclusion at the monastery o
1 CONC f Dömös founded by himself until his death, but his son would succeed as king of Hungary.
1 CONT
1 CONT Álmos was the last duke of Nitra (in Hungarian Nyitra), his removal also marks the end of the Nitrian Frontier Duchy and thus a full integration of the complete territory of today's Slovakia into Hungary.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Family
1 CONT On August 21, 1104 Álmos married Predslava, the daughter of Svyatopolk II of Kiev and has children:
