0 @N6000000002187828754@ NOTE Henry I the Bearded
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry I the Bearded (Polish: Henryk I Brodaty; German: Heinrich I der Bärtige,; 1163 - March 19, 1238), of the Silesian line of the Piast dynasty, was Duke of Lower Silesia from 1201. He was later also Duke of Lesser Poland and th
1 CONC us senior prince of all Poland from 1232 until his death.
1 CONT
1 CONT Born in Glogów, Silesia, in southwestern Poland, he married Hedwig of Andechs (Polish: Jadwiga). His son and successor, Duke Henry II the Pious, would later be killed battling the Mongols at Legnica.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry I had succeeded his father, Duke Boleslaw I the Tall, who had received the ducal position following an 1163 intervention, in a succession dispute, by Holy Roman Emperor Frederick I Barbarossa.
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry I strove to reunite the provinces of fragmented Poland, and succeeded in bringing under his authority Silesia, Lesser Poland and part of Greater Poland.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT History of Poland (966-1385) 
1 CONT Dukes of Silesia 
1 CONT
