0 @N6000000002187639867@ NOTE Richeza of Lotharingia
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Blessed Richeza of Lotharingia 
1 CONT
1 CONT Richeza of Lotharingia(Jan Matejko 1838-1893) 
1 CONT Queen of Poland, of the Ezzonian dynasty 
1 CONT Born 995 or 1000 
1 CONT Died 21 March 1063, Saalfeld 
1 CONT Venerated in Roman Catholicism 
1 CONT Major shrine Cologne Germany 
1 CONT Feast 21 March 
1 CONT  Saints Portal 
1 CONT
1 CONT Richeza of Lotharingia (also called Richenza and Rixa)(born between 995 and 1000–March 21, 1063 in Saalfeld) was the Queen of Poland as the wife of King Mieszko II.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the daughter of the Count Palatine Ezzo of Lotharingia (Ezzonen) and Mathilde of Saxony (daughter of emperor Otto II and Theophanu). Her mother, Mathilde of Saxony, was the sister of Otto III, Holy Roman Emperor.
1 CONT
1 CONT She became a nun after 7 September 1047 and is buried in Cologne.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her feast day is celebrated on March 21.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Source
1 CONT Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Line 147-22 
1 CONT
1 CONT Richeza of LotharingiaWikimedia Commons has media related to: 
1 CONT Richensa of Lotharingia(Wojchiech Gerson 1891)
