0 @N6000000004533185687@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Matthias I (1119 – May 13, 1176) was Duke of Lorraine from 1138 to hisdeath. He married Bertha of Hohenstaufen, daughter of Frederick II,Duke of Swabia and sister of Frederick Barbarossa, Holy Roman Emperor.They had the following 
1 CONC issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT Duke Simon II of Lorraine (d.1205)
1 CONT Duke Frederick I of Lorraine (d.1206)
1 CONT Judith of Lorraine (d.1173), married Etienne II, count d'Auxonne
1 CONT Alice of Lorraine (d.1200), married to Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy
1 CONT Thierry, bishop and elector of Metz (d.1181)
1 CONT Matthias, count of Toul (d.1208)
0 @N6000000005598872135@ NOTE Matthias I (1119 - May 13, 1176) was the duke of Lorraine from 1138 t o his death as the eldest son and successor of Simon I and Adelaide o f Supplinburg. Like his forefathers going back to Thierry II and event o Adalbert, he was 
1 CONC a stern supporter of the king of Germany and HolyRo man Emperor. This loyalty transcended dynasties: his fathers had follo wed the Salians, his mother was a niece of the Supplinburger Emperor L othair II, and he himself married Ju
1 CONC dith (sometimes called Bertha), da ughter of Frederick II, Duke of Swabia, and therefore niece of the Hoh enstaufen king Conrad III and sister of Frederick Barbarossa, future e mperor.
1 CONT
1 CONT He accompanied Barbarossa on a number of important occasions, includin g his imperial coronation by Pope Adrian IV in Rome, 1155. He assiste d the emperor in his wars against Adrian and his successor Alexander I II and the kings o
1 CONC f France and Sicily. He extended his own ducal demes ne at the expense of the bishop of Toul, but was an important donor t o the Church and founder of abbeys.
1 CONT
1 CONT He died in 1176 and was interred in his abbey of Clairlieu in Villers- lès-Nancy. By his Hohenstaufen marriage (1138), he had:
1 CONT
1 CONT Simon (d.1205), his successor in Lorraine
1 CONT Frederick (d.1206), count of Bitche and his nephew's successor
1 CONT Judith (d.1173), married Stephen II, count of Auxonne (1170)
1 CONT Alice (d.1200), married Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy
1 CONT Thierry (d.1181), bishop of Metz (1174-1179)
1 CONT Matthias (d.1208), count of Toul
1 CONT Unnamed daughter who died young
